\id 1CH - Brenton English Septuagint 
\h Chronicles I 
\toc1 Chronicles I 
\toc2 Chronicles I 
\toc3 1 Chr. 
\mt1 CHRONICLES I.  
\c 1
\s1 From Adam to Abraham
\p \v 1 \sc Adam\sc*, Seth, Enosh,
\v 2 and Cainan, Mahalalel, Jared,
\v 3 Enoch, Methuselah, Lamech,
\v 4 Noah:
\li1 the sons of Noah, Shem, Ham, Japheth.
\b
\li1 \v 5 The sons of Japheth,
\li2 Gomer, Magog, Madai, Javan, Elishah, Tubal, Mosoch, and Thiras.
\li2 \v 6 And the sons of Gomer, Ashkenaz, and Riphath, and Togarmah.
\li2 \v 7 And the sons of Javan, Elishah, and Tarshish, the Kittites, and Rodanites.
\b
\li1 \v 8 And the sons of Ham,
\li2 Cush, and Mizraim, Put and Canaan.
\li2 \v 9 And the sons of Cush, Saba, and Havilah, and Sabatha, and Raamah, and Sabteca:
\li2 and the sons of Raamah, Saba, and Dedan.
\li2 \v 10 And Cush begot Nimrod: he began to be a mighty hunter on the earth.
\b
\li1 \v 17 The sons of Shem,
\li2 Elam, and Asshur,
\li2 \v 24 and Arphaxad, Shelah,
\v 25 Eber, Peleg, Reu,
\v 26 Seruch, Nahor, Terah,
\v 27 Abraham.
\s1 The Descendants of Abraham
\p \v 28 And the sons of Abraham, Isaac, and Ishmael.
\b
\q1 \v 29 And these \add are\add* their generations:
\li1 the first-born of Ishmael, Nebaioth, and Kedar, Adbeel, Mibsam,
\v 30 Mishma, Iduma, Masse, Hadad, Thæman,
\v 31 Jetur, Naphish, Kedemah: these \add are\add* the sons of Ishmael.
\b
\li1 \v 32 And the sons of Keturah Abraham's concubine:—and she bore him
\li2 Zimran, Jokshan, Midian, Medan, Ishbak, Shuah:
\li1 and the sons of Jokshan;
\li2 Dedan, and Sabai;
\b
\li1 \v 33 and the sons of Midian;
\li2 Ephah, and Hepher, and Enoch, and Abida, and Eldaah; all these \add were\add* the sons of Keturah.
\b
\li1 \v 34 And Abraham begot Isaac:
\li2 and the sons of Isaac \add were\add* Jacob, and Esau.
\s1 The Descendants of Esau
\li1 \v 35 The sons of Esau,
\li2 Eliphaz, and Reuel, and Jeul, and Jalam, and Korah.
\li2 \v 36 The sons of Eliphaz: Thæman, and Omar, Sophar, and Gatam, and Kenez, and Timna, and Amalek.
\li2 \v 37 And the sons of Reuel, Nahath, Zerah, Shammah, and Moze.
\s1 The Descendants of Seir
\li1 \v 38 The sons of Seir,
\li2 Lotan, Shobal, Zibeon, Ana, Dishon, Osar, and Disan.
\li2 \v 39 And the sons of Lotan, Chorri, and Heman; and the sister of Lotan \add was\add* Timna.
\li2 \v 40 The sons of Shobal; Alon, Machanath, Tæbel, Shepho, and Onan:
\li2 and the sons of Zibeon; Aiah, and Anah.
\li2 \v 41 The sons of Anah, Dishon:
\li2 and the sons of Dishon; Hemdan, and Asebon, and Ithran, and Charran.
\li2 \v 42 And the sons of Ezer, Bilhan, and Zaavan, and Akan:
\li2 the sons of Disan, Uz, and Aran.
\s1 The Kings of Edom
\p \v 43 And these \add are\add* their kings,
\li1 Bela the son of Beor; and the name of his city \add was\add* Dinhabah.
\b
\li1 \v 44 And Bela died, and Jobab the son of Zerah of Bozrah reigned in his stead.
\b
\li1 \v 45 And Jobab died, and Asom of the land of the Temanites reigned in his stead.
\b
\li1 \v 46 And Asom died, and Hadad the son of Bedad reigned in his stead, who struck Midian in the plain of Moab: and the name of his city \add was\add* Avith.
\b
\li1 \v 47 And Hadad died, and Samlah of Masrekah reigned in his stead.
\b
\li1 \v 48 And Samlah died, and Saul of Rehoboth by the river reigned in his stead.
\b
\li1 \v 49 And Saul died, and Baal-hanan son of Achbor reigned in his stead.
\b
\li1 \v 50 And Baal-hanan died, and Hadad son of Bedad reigned in his stead; and the name of his city \add was\add* Pau.
\b
\p \v 51 The princes of Edom: prince Timna, prince Alvah, prince Jeths,
\v 52 prince Oholibamah, prince Elah, prince Pinon,
\v 53 prince Kenez, prince Thæman, prince Mibzar, prince Magdiel,
\v 54 prince Iram. These \add are\add* the princes of Edom.
\c 2  
\p
\v 1 These \add are\add* the names of the sons of Israel;  
\v 2 Reuben, Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar, Zebulun, Dan, Joseph, Benjamin, Naphtali, Gad, Aser.   
\p
\v 3 The sons of Judah; Er, Onan, Shelah. \add These\add* three were born to him of the daughter of Shua the Canaanite woman: and Er, the first-born of Judah, \add was\add* wicked before the Lord, and he slew him.  
\v 4 And Tamar his daughter-in-law bore to him Phares, and Zerah: all the sons of Judah \add were\add* five.   
\p
\v 5 The sons of Phares, Hezron, and Jemuel.  
\v 6 And the sons of Zerah, Zimri, and Ethan, and Heman, and Calcol, and Dara, \add in\add* all five.   
\p
\v 7 And the sons of Carmi; Sachar the troubler of Israel, who was disobedient in the accursed thing.  
\v 8 And the sons of Ethan; Azarias,  
\v 9 and the sons of Hezron who were born to him; Jerameel, and Aram, and Caleb.   
\p
\v 10 And Aram begot Aminadab, and Aminadab begot Nahshon, chief of the house of Judah.  
\v 11 And Nahshon begot Salmon, and Salmon begot Boaz,  
\v 12 and Boaz begot Obed, and Obed begot Jesse.  
\v 13 And Jesse begot his first-born Eliab, Aminadab \add was\add* the second, Samaa the third,  
\v 14 Nethanel the fourth, Raddai the fifth,  
\v 15 Asam the sixth, David the seventh.  
\v 16 And their sister \add was\add* Zeruiah, and \add another\add* Abigail: and the sons of Zeruiah \add were\add* Abishai, and Joab, and Asahel, three.  
\v 17 And Abigail bore Amasa: and the father of Amasa \add was\add* Jothor the Ishmaelite.   
\p
\v 18 And Caleb the son of Hezron took Azubah to wife, and Jerioth: and these \add were\add* her sons; Jesher, and Shobab, and Ardon.  
\v 19 And Azubah died; and Caleb took to himself Ephrath, and she bore to him Or.  
\v 20 And Or begot Uri, and Uri begot Bezalel.  
\v 21 And after this Hezron went in to the daughter of Machir the father of Gilead, and he took her when he was sixty-five years old; and she bore him Seruch.  
\v 22 And Seruch begot Jair, and he had twenty-three cities in Gilead.  
\v 23 And he took Geshur and Aram, the towns of Jair from them; \add with\add* Kenath and its towns, sixty cities. All these \add belonged to\add* the sons of Machir the father of Gilead.  
\v 24 And after the death of Hezron, Caleb came to Ephratha; and the wife of Hezron \add was\add* Abijah; and she bore him Ashhur the father of Tekoa.   
\p
\v 25 And the sons of Jerameel the first-born of Hezron \add were\add*, the first-born Ram, and Bunah, and Aram, and Asan his brother.  
\v 26 And Jerameel had another wife, and her name \add was\add* Atarah: she is the mother of Onam.  
\v 27 And the sons of Ram the first-born of Jerameel were Maaz, and Jamin, and Eker.  
\v 28 And the sons of Onam were, Samai, and Jada: and the sons of Samai; Nadab, and Abishur.  
\v 29 And the name of the wife of Abishur \add was\add* Abihail, and she bore him Ahban, and Molid.  
\v 30 And the sons of Nadab; Seled and Appaim; and Seled died without children.  
\v 31 And the sons of Appaim, Ishi; and the sons of Ishi, Sheshan; and the sons of Sheshan, Ahlai.  
\v 32 And the sons of Ahlai, Achisamas, Jeths, Jonathan: and Jeths died childless.  
\v 33 And the sons of Jonathan; Peleth, and Zaza. These were the sons of Jerameel.   
\p
\v 34 And Sheshan had no sons, but daughters. And Sheshan had an Egyptian servant, and his name \add was\add* Jarha.  
\v 35 And Sheshan gave his daughter to Jarha his servant to wife; and she bore him Attai.  
\v 36 And Attai begot Nathan, and Nathan begot Zabad,  
\v 37 and Zabad begot Ephlal, and Ephlal begot Obed.  
\v 38 And Obed begot Jehu, and Jehu begot Azarias,  
\v 39 and Azarias begot Helez, and Helez begot Elasah,  
\v 40 and Elasah begot Sismai, and Sismai begot Shallum,  
\v 41 and Shallum begot Jekamiah, and Jekamiah begot Elishama, and Elishama begot Ishmael.   
\p
\v 42 And the sons of Caleb the brother of Jerameel \add were\add*, Marisa his first-born, he \add is\add* the father of Ziph:—and the sons of Marisa the father of Hebron.  
\v 43 And the sons of Hebron; Korah, and Tappuah, and Rekem, and Samaa.  
\v 44 And Samaa begot Raham the father of Jorkeam: and Jorkeam begot Samai.  
\v 45 And his son \add was\add* Maon: and Maon \add is\add* the father of Beth-zur.  
\v 46 And Ephah the concubine of Caleb bore Aram, and Moza, and Gazez.  
\v 47 And the sons of Jahdai \add were\add* Regem, and Jotham, and Sogar, and Pelet, and Ephah, and Shaaph.  
\v 48 And Caleb's concubine Maacah bore Sheber, and Tirhanah.  
\v 49 She bore also Shaaph the father of Madmannah, and Sheva the father of Machbenah, and the father of Gibea: and the daughter of Caleb \add was\add* Acsah.   
\p
\v 50 These were the sons of Caleb: the sons of Or the first-born of Ephratha; Shobal the father of Kiriath-jearim,  
\v 51 Salma the father of Bethlehem, Hareph the father of Bæthalaem, and Hareph the father of Beth-gader.  
\v 52 And the sons of Shobal the father of Kiriath-jearim were Araa, and Æsi, and Ammanith,  
\v 53 and Umasphaë, cities of Jair; Ithrites, and Puthites, and Shumathites, and Mishraites; from these went forth the Zorathites, and the sons of Eshtaolites.  
\v 54 The sons of Salma; Bæthalaem, the Netophathite, Ataroth of the house of Joab, and half of the family of Manahathites, Zorites.  
\v 55 The families of the scribes dwelling in Jabez; Tirathites, and Shimeathites, and Sucathites, these \add are\add* the Kenites that came of Hammath, the father of the house of Rechab.   
\c 3  
\p
\v 1 Now these were the sons of David that were born to him in Hebron; the first-born Amnon, \add born\add* of Ahinoam the Jezreelite; the second Daniel, of Abigail the Carmelite.  
\v 2 The third, Absalom, the son of Maacah the daughter of Talmai king of Geshur; the fourth, Adonijah the son of Haggith.  
\v 3 The fifth, Shephatiah, \add the son\add* of Abital; the sixth, Ithream, \add born\add* of Eglah his wife.  
\v 4 Six were born to him in Hebron; and he reigned there seven years and six months: and he reigned thirty-three years in Jerusalem.  
\v 5 And these were born to him in Jerusalem; Samaa, Shobab, Nathan, and Solomon; four \add of\add* Bathsheba the daughter of Ammiel:  
\v 6 and Ibhar, and Elisa, and Eliphelet,  
\v 7 and Nogah, and Nepheg, and Japhia,  
\v 8 and Helisama, and Eliada, and Eliphelet, nine.  
\v 9 All \add these were\add* the sons of David, besides the sons of the concubines, and \add there was also\add* Tamar their sister.   
\p
\v 10 The sons of Solomon; Rehoboam, Abijah his son, Asa his son, Josaphat his son,  
\v 11 Joram his son, Ahaziah his son, Joash his son,  
\v 12 Amaziah his son, Azarias his son, Jotham his son,  
\v 13 Ahaz his son, Hezekiah his son, Manasseh his son,  
\v 14 Amon his son, Josia his son.  
\v 15 And the sons of Josia; the first-born Joanan, the second Joakim, the third Zedekiah, the fourth Shallum.  
\v 16 And the sons of Joakim; Jeconiah his son, Zedekiah his son.  
\v 17 And the sons of Jeconiah; Asir, Shealtiel his son,  
\v 18 Malchiram, and Phadaias, and Shenazzar, and Jekimia, and Hoshama, and Nedabiah.   
\p
\v 19 And the sons of Phadaias; Zerubbabel, and Semei: and the sons of Zerubbabel; Meshullam, and Hananiah, and Shelomith \add was\add* their sister.  
\v 20 And Hashubah, and Ohel, and Berechiah, and Hasadiah, and Jushab-hesed, five.   
\p
\v 21 And the sons of Hananiah, Pelatiah, and Jeshaiah his son, Rephaiah his son, Arnan his son, Obadiah his son, Shecaniah his son.  
\v 22 And the son of Shecaniah; Shemaiah: and the sons of Shemaiah; Hattush, and Joel, and Berri and Neariah, and Shaphat, six.   
\p
\v 23 And the sons of Neariah: Elioenai, and Hizkiah, and Azrikam, three.   
\p
\v 24 And the sons of Elioenai; Hodaviah, and Eliashib, and Pelaiah, and Akub, and Joanan, and Delaiah, and Anan, seven.   
\c 4  
\p
\v 1 And the sons of Judah; Phares, Hezron, and Carmi, and Or, Shobal,  
\v 2 and Reaiah his son; and Shobal begot Jahath; and Jahath begot Ahumai, and Lahad: these \add are\add* the generations of the Arathites.  
\v 3 And these \add are\add* the sons of Etam; Jezreel and Ishma, and Idbash: and their sister's name \add was\add* Hazzelelponi.  
\v 4 And Penuel the father of Gedor, and Jazer the father of Hushah: these \add are\add* the sons of Or, the first-born of Ephratha, the father of Bæthalaen.   
\p
\v 5 And Ashhur the father of Tekoa had two wives, Helah and Naarah.  
\v 6 And Helah bore to him Ahuzzam, and Hepher, and Thæman, and Haahashtari: all these \add were\add* the sons of Helah.  
\v 7 And the sons of Naarah; Zereth, and Zohar, and Ethnan.  
\v 8 And Koz begot Anub, and Sabatha, and the progeny of the brother of Rechab, the son of Harum.  
\v 9 And Jabez was more famous than his brothers; and his mother called his name Jabez, saying, I have born as a sorrowful one.  
\v 10 And Jabez called on the God of Israel, saying, O that you would indeed bless me, and enlarge my coasts, and that your hand might be with me, and that you would make me know that you will not grieve me! And God granted him all that he asked.   
\p
\v 11 And Caleb the father of Acsah begot Machir; he \add was\add* the father of Assathon.  
\v 12 He begot Bathraias, and Besseë, and Thæman the founder of the city of Ir-nahash the brother of Eselom the Kenezite: these \add were\add* the men of Rechab.  
\v 13 And the sons of Kenez; Othniel, and Seraiah: and the sons of Othniel; Hathath.  
\v 14 And Meonothai begot Ophrah: and Seraiah begot Jobab, the father of Ageaddair, for they were artificers.  
\v 15 And the sons of Caleb the son of Jephunneh; Er, Ada, and Naam: and the sons of Ada, Kenez.  
\v 16 And the sons of Jehallelel, Ziph, and Ziphah, and Tiria, and Asarel.  
\v 17 And the sons of Ezrah; Jeths, Mered, and Apher, and Jalon: and Jeths begot Miriam, and Semei, and Ishbah the father of Eshtemoa.  
\v 18 And his wife, that \add is\add* Bithiah, bore Jared the father of Gedor, and Heber the father of Soco, and Jekuthiel the father of Zanoah: and these \add are\add* the sons of Bithiah the daughter of Pharaoh, whom Mored took.  
\v 19 And the sons of the wife of Hodiah the sister of Naham the father of Keilah; Garmite, and Eshtemoa the Maacathite.  
\v 20 And the sons of Shimon; Amnon, and Ana the son of Phana, and Inon: and the sons of Sei, Zoan, and the sons of Zoab.   
\p
\v 21 The sons of Shelah the son of Judah; Er the father of Lecah, and Laadah the father of Marisa, and the offspring of the family of Ephrathabac \add belonging to\add* the house of Esoba.  
\v 22 And Joakim, and the men of Cozeba, and Joash, and Saraph, who dwelt in Moab, and he changed their names to Abederin and Athukiim.  
\v 23 These \add are\add* the potters who dwelt in Netaim and Gederah with the king: they grew strong in his kingdom, and dwelt there.   
\p
\v 24 The sons of Semeon; Nemuel, and Jamin, Jarib, Zerah, Saul:  
\v 25 Salem his son, Mibsam his son, Mishma his son:  
\v 26 Hammuel his son, Sabud his son, Zacchur his son, Semei his son.  
\v 27 Semei \add had\add* sixteen sons, and six daughters; and his brothers had not many sons, nor did all their families multiply as the sons of Judah.  
\v 28 And they dwelt in Bathsheba, and Molada, and in Esersual,  
\v 29 and in Balaa, and in Æsem, and in Tholad,  
\v 30 and in Bethuel, and in Herma, and in Ziklag,  
\v 31 and in Bæthmarimoth, and Hemisuseosin, and the house of Baruseorim: these \add were\add* their cities until \add the time of\add* king David.  
\v 32 And their villages \add were\add* Ætan, and En, Remnon, and Thocca, and Æsar, five cities.  
\v 33 And all their villages \add were\add* round about these cities, as far as Baal: this \add was\add* their possession, and their distribution.  
\v 34 And Mosobab, and Jemoloch, and Josia the son of Amasia;  
\v 35 and Joel, and Jehu the son of Asabia, the son of Sarau, the son of Jahzeel;  
\v 36 and Eliehoenai, and Jocaba, and Jasuia, and Asaia, and Jediel, and Ishmael, and Benaiah;  
\v 37 and Zuza the son of Saphai, the son of Alon, the son of Jedia, the son of Semri, the son of Samaias.  
\v 38 These went by the names of princes in their families, and they increased abundantly in their fathers' households.   
\p
\v 39 And they went till they came to Gerar, to the east of Gai, to seek pasture for their cattle.  
\v 40 And they found abundant and good pastures, and the land before them \add was\add* wide, and \add there was\add* peace and quietness; for \add there were\add* Shammah of the children of Ham who dwelt there before.  
\v 41 And these who are written by name came in the days of Hezekiah king of Judah, and they struck the people's houses, and the Minæans whom they found there, and utterly destroyed them until this day: and they dwelt in their place, because \add there was\add* pasture there for their cattle.  
\v 42 And Shammah of them, \add even\add* of the sons of Simeon, went to mount Seir, \add even\add* five hundred men; and Phalaettia, and Neariah, and Rephaiah, and Oziel, sons of Jesi, \add were\add* their rulers.  
\v 43 And they struck the remnant that were left of Amalek, until this day.   
\c 5  
\p
\v 1 And the sons of Reuben the first-born of Israel (for he \add was\add* the first-born; but because of his going up to his father's couch, \add his father\add* gave his blessing to his son Joseph, \add even\add* the son of Israel; and he was not reckoned as first-born;  
\v 2 for Judas \add was\add* very mighty even among his brothers, and one was to be a ruler out of him: but the blessing \add was\add* Joseph's).  
\v 3 The sons of Reuben the first-born of Israel; Enoch, and Phallus, Hezron, and Carmi.  
\v 4 The sons of Joel; Semei, and Benaiah his son: and the sons of Gug the son of Semei.  
\v 5 His son \add was\add* Micha, his son Reaiah, his son Joel,  
\v 6 his son Beerah, whom Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria carried away captive: he \add is\add* the chief of the Reubenites.   
\p
\v 7 And his brothers in his family, in their distribution according to their generations; the chief, Joel, and Zechariah.  
\v 8 And Bela the son of Azaz, the son of Sama, the son of Joel: he dwelt in Aroer, and even to Nebo, and Baal-meon.  
\v 9 And he dwelt eastward to the borders of the wilderness, from the river Euphrates: for they had much cattle in the land of Gilead.  
\v 10 And in the days of Saul they made war upon the sojourners \add in the land\add*; and they fell into their hands, all of them dwelling in their tents eastward of Gilead.   
\p
\v 11 The sons of Gad dwelt over against them in the land of Bashan even to Salecah.  
\v 12 Joel the first-born, and Shapham the second, and Janin the scribe in Bashan.  
\v 13 And their brothers according to the houses of their fathers; Michael, Meshullam, and Sebee, and Jorai, and Jacan, and Zia, and Obed, seven.  
\v 14 These \add are\add* the sons of Abihail the son of Uri, the son of Huri, the son of Gilead, the son of Michael, the son of Jeshishai, the son of Jahdo, the son of Buz,  
\v 15 \add who was\add* the brother of the son of Abdiel, the son of Guni, \add he was\add* chief of the house of their families.  
\v 16 They dwelt in Gilead, in Bashan, and in their villages, and \add in\add* all the country round about Sharon to the border.  
\v 17 The enumeration of \add them\add* all took place in the days of Jotham king of Judah, and in the days of Jeroboam king of Israel.   
\p
\v 18 The sons of Reuben and Gad, and the half-tribe of Manasseh, of mighty men, bearing shields and sword, and bending the bow, and skilled in war, \add were\add* forty and four thousand and seven hundred and sixty, going forth to battle.  
\v 19 And they made war with the Hagrites, and Itureans, and Naphiseans, and Nadabeans,  
\v 20 and they prevailed against them: and the Hagrites were given into their hands, \add they\add* and all their tents: for they cried to God in the battle, and he hearkened to them, because they trusted on him.  
\v 21 And they took captive their store; five thousand camels, and two hundred and fifty thousand sheep, two thousand asses, and a hundred thousand men.  
\v 22 For many fell slain, because the war \add was\add* of God. And they dwelt in their place until the captivity.   
\p
\v 23 And the half-tribe of Manasseh dwelt from Bashan to Baal, Baal-hermon, and Senir, and \add to\add* the mount Hermon: and they increased in Lebanon.  
\v 24 And these were the heads of the houses of their families; Hepher, and Sei, and Eliel, and Jeremiah, and Hodaviah, and Jediel, mighty men of valour, men of renown, heads of the houses of their families.   
\p
\v 25 But they rebelled against the God of their fathers, and went a-whoring after the gods of the nations of the land, whom God cast out from before them.  
\v 26 And the God of Israel stirred up the spirit of Pul king of Assyria, and the spirit of Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria, and carried away Reuben and Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh, and brought them to Halah, and Habor, and to the river Gozan, until this day.   
\p
\v 27 The sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.  
\v 28 And the sons of Kohath; Amram, and Issaar, Hebron, and Oziel.  
\v 29 And the sons of Amram; Aaron, and Moses, and Miriam: and the sons of Aaron; Nadab, and Abiud, Eleazar, and Ithamar.  
\v 30 Eleazar begot Phinehas, Phinehas begot Abishua;  
\v 31 Abishua begot Bukki, and Bukki begot Uzza;  
\v 32 Uzza begot Zerahiah, Zerahiah begot Meraioth;  
\v 33 and Meraioth begot Amaria, and Amaria begot Ahitub;  
\v 34 and Ahitub begot Zadok, and Zadok begot Ahimaaz;  
\v 35 and Ahimaaz begot Azarias, and Azarias begot Joanan;  
\v 36 and Joanan begot Azarias: he ministered as priest in the house which Solomon built in Jerusalem.  
\v 37 And Azarias begot Amaria, and Amaria begot Ahitub;  
\v 38 and Ahitub begot Zadok, and Zadok begot Salom;  
\v 39 and Salom begot Hilkiah, and Hilkiah begot Azarias;  
\v 40 and Azarias begot Seraiah, and Seraiah begot Jehozadak.  
\v 41 And Jehozadak went into captivity with Judah and Jerusalem under Nebuchadnezzar.   
\c 6  
\p
\v 1 The sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.  
\v 2 And these \add are\add* the names of the sons of Gershon; Libni, and Semei.  
\v 3 The sons of Kohath; Amram, and Issaar, Hebron, and Oziel.  
\v 4 The sons of Merari; Mahli and Mushi: and these \add are\add* the families of Levi, according to their families.  
\v 5 To Gershon—to Libni his son—\add were born\add* Jahath his son, Zimmah his son,  
\v 6 Joab his son, Eri his son, Zerah his son, Jeatherai his son.  
\v 7 The sons of Kohath; Aminadab his son, Korah his son, Aser his son;  
\v 8 Elkanah his son, Ebiasaph his son, Aser his son:  
\v 9 Tahath his son, Uriel his son, Ozia his son, Saul his son.  
\v 10 And the sons of Elkanah; Amasai, and Ahimoth.  
\v 11 Elkanah his son, Zophai his son, Nahath his son;  
\v 12 Eliab his son, Jeroboam his son, Elkanah his son.  
\v 13 The sons of Samuel; the first-born Sani, and Abijah.  
\v 14 The sons of Merari; Mahli, Libni his son, Semei his son, Azzan his son;  
\v 15 Samaa his son, Haggiah his son, Asaiah his son.   
\p
\v 16 And these \add were the men\add* whom David set over the service of the singers in the house of the Lord when the ark was at rest.  
\v 17 And they ministered in front of the tabernacle of witness \add playing\add* on instruments, until Solomon built the house of the Lord in Jerusalem; and they stood according to their order for their services.   
\p
\v 18 And these \add were the men\add* that stood, and their sons, of the sons of Kohath: Heman the psalm singer, son of Joel, the son of Samuel,  
\v 19 the son of Elkanah, the son of Jeroboam, the son of Eliel, the son of Toah,  
\v 20 the son of Suph, the son of Elkanah, the son of Mahath, the son of Amathi,  
\v 21 the son of Elkanah, the son of Joel, the son of Azarias, the son of Zephaniah,  
\v 22 the son of Tahath, the son of Aser, the son of Abiasaph, the son of Korah,  
\v 23 the son of Isaar, the son of Kohath, the son of Levi, the son of Israel.  
\v 24 And his brother Asaph, who stood at his right hand; Asaph the son of Barachias, the son of Samaa,  
\v 25 the son of Michael, the son of Baaseiah, the son of Malchijah,  
\v 26 the son of Ethni, the son of Zerah,  
\v 27 the son of Adaiah, the son of Ethan, the son of Zammam, the son of Semei,  
\v 28 the son of Jeeth, the son of Gershon, the son of Levi.  
\v 29 And the sons of Merari their brothers on the left hand: Ethan the son of Kishi, the son of Abai, the son of Malluch,  
\v 30 the son of Hashabiah,  
\v 31 the son of Amaziah, the son of Bani, the son of Shemer,  
\v 32 the son of Mahli, the son of Mushi, the son of Merari, the son of Levi.  
\v 33 And their brothers according to the houses of their fathers, \add were\add* the Levites who were appointed to all the work of ministration of the tabernacle of the house of God.   
\p
\v 34 And Aaron and his sons \add were\add* to burn incense on the altar of whole-burnt-offerings, and on the altar of incense, for all the ministry \add in\add* the holy of holies, and to make atonement for Israel, according to all things that Moses the servant of the Lord commanded.  
\v 35 And these \add are\add* the sons of Aaron; Eleazar his son, Phinehas his son, Abishua his son,  
\v 36 Bukki his son, Uzza his son, Seraiah his son,  
\v 37 Meraioth his son, Amaria his son, Ahitub his son,  
\v 38 Zadok his son, Ahimaaz his son.   
\p
\v 39 And these \add are\add* their residences in their villages, in their coasts, to the sons of Aaron, to their family the Caathites: for they had the lot.  
\v 40 And they gave them Hebron in the land of Judah, and its suburbs round about it.  
\v 41 But the fields of the city, and its villages, they gave to Caleb the son of Jephunneh.  
\v 42 And to the sons of Aaron they gave the cities of refuge, \add even\add* Hebron, and Lobna and her suburbs round about, and Selna and her suburbs, and Esthamo and her suburbs,  
\v 43 and Jethar and her suburbs, and Dabir and her suburbs,  
\v 44 and Asan and her suburbs, and Bæthsamys and her suburbs:  
\v 45 and of the tribe of Benjamin Gabai and her suburbs, and Galemath and her suburbs, and Anathoth and her suburbs: all their cities \add were\add* thirteen cities according to their families.   
\p
\v 46 And to the sons of Kohath that were left of their families, \add there were given\add* out of the tribe, \add namely\add*, out of the half-tribe of Manasseh, by lot, ten cities.  
\v 47 And to the sons of Gershon according to their families \add there were given\add* thirteen cities of the tribe of Issachar, of the tribe of Aser, of the tribe of Naphtali, of the tribe of Manasseh in Bashan.  
\v 48 And to the sons of Merari according to their families \add there were given\add*, by lot, twelve cities of the tribe of Reuben, of the tribe of Gad, \add and\add* of the tribe of Zebulun.  
\v 49 So the children of Israel gave to the Levites the cities and their suburbs.  
\v 50 And they gave by lot out of the tribe of the children of Judah, and out of the tribe of the children of Simeon, and out of the tribe of the children of Benjamin, these cities which they call by name.   
\p
\v 51 And \add to the members\add* of the families of the sons of Kohath there were also given the cities of their borders out of the tribe of Ephraim.  
\v 52 And they gave them the cities of refuge, Shechem and her suburbs in mount Ephraim, and Gezer and her suburbs,  
\v 53 and Jokmeam and her suburbs, and Beth-horon and her suburbs,  
\v 54 and Aijalon and her suburbs, and Gath-rimmon and her suburbs:  
\v 55 and of the half-tribe of Manasseh Aner and her suburbs, and Bileam and her suburbs, to the sons of Kohath that were left, according to \add each several\add* family.   
\p
\v 56 To the sons of Gershon from the families of the half-tribe of Manasseh \add they gave\add* Golan of Bashan and her suburbs, and Ashtaroth and her suburbs.  
\v 57 And out of the tribe of Issachar, Kedesh and her suburbs, and Daberath and her suburbs, and Dabor and her suburbs,  
\v 58 and Ramoth, and Enan and her suburbs.  
\v 59 And of the tribe of Aser; Mashal and her suburbs, and Abdon and her suburbs,  
\v 60 and Hukok and her suburbs, and Rehob and her suburbs.  
\v 61 And of the tribe of Naphtali; Kedesh in Galilee and her suburbs, and Hammon and her suburbs, and Kiriathaim and her suburbs.   
\p
\v 62 To the sons of Merari that were left, \add they gave\add* out of the tribe of Zebulun Rimmono and her suburbs, and Tabor and her suburbs:  
\v 63 out of \add the country\add* beyond Jordan; Jericho westward of Jordan: out of the tribe of Reuben; Bosor in the wilderness and her suburbs, and Jahzah and her suburbs,  
\v 64 and Kedemoth and her suburbs, and Mephaath and her suburbs.  
\v 65 Out of the tribe of Gad; Rammoth Gilead and her suburbs, and Mahanaim and her suburbs,  
\v 66 and Esebon and her suburbs, and Jazer and her suburbs.   
\c 7  
\p
\v 1 And \add as\add* to the sons of Issachar, \add they were\add* Tola, and Puvah, and Jashub, and Shimron, four.  
\v 2 And the sons of Tola; Uzza, Rephaiah, and Jeriel, and Jahmai, and Ibsam, and Samuel, chiefs of their fathers' houses \add belonging to\add* Tola, men of might according to their generations; their number in the days of David \add was\add* twenty and two thousand and six hundred.  
\v 3 And the sons of Uzza; Izrahiah: and the sons of Izrahiah; Michael, Obadiah, and Joel, and Isshiah, five, all rulers.   
\p
\v 4 And with them, according to their generations, according to the houses of their families, \add were men\add* mighty to set \add armies\add* in array for war, thirty and six thousand, for they had multiplied \add their\add* wives and children.  
\v 5 And their brothers among all the families of Issachar, also mighty men, \add were\add* eighty-seven thousand—\add this was\add* the number of them all.   
\p
\v 6 The sons of Benjamin; Bela, and Becher, and Jediel, three.  
\v 7 And the sons of Bela; Esebon, and Uzza, and Oziel, and Jeremoth, and Uri, five; heads of houses of families, mighty men; and their number \add was\add* twenty and two thousand and thirty-four.  
\v 8 And the sons of Becher; Zemirah, and Joash, and Eliezer, and Elioenai, and Amaria, and Jeremoth, and Abiud, and Anathoth, and Alems: all these \add were\add* the sons of Becher.  
\v 9 And their number according to their generations, (\add they were\add* chiefs of their fathers' houses, men of might), \add was\add* twenty thousand and two hundred.  
\v 10 And the sons of Jediel; Balaan: and the sons of Balaan; Jaüs, and Benjamin, and Aoth, and Chenaanah, and Zethan, and Tharsi, and Ahishahar.  
\v 11 All these \add were\add* the sons of Jediel, chiefs of their families, men of might, seventeen thousand and two hundred, going forth to war with might.  
\v 12 And Shuppim, and Apphin, and the sons of Or, Asom, whose son \add was\add* Aher.   
\p
\v 13 The sons of Naphtali; Jaasiel, Guni, and Aser, and Shallum, his sons, Balam his son.   
\p
\v 14 The sons of Manasseh; Asriel, whom his Syrian concubine bore; and she bore to him also Machir the father of Gilead.  
\v 15 And Machir took a wife for Apphin and Shuppim, and his sister's name was Moöcha; and the name of the second \add son\add* was Sapphaad; and to Sapphaad were born daughters.  
\v 16 And Moöcha the wife of Machir bore a son, and called his name Phares; and his brother's name \add was\add* Surus; his sons \add were\add* Ulam, and Rocom.  
\v 17 And the sons of Ulam; Badam. These \add were\add* the sons of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh.  
\v 18 And his sister Malechs bore Isud, and Abiezer, and Maela.  
\v 19 And the sons of Semira were, Aim, and Shechem, and Lakim, and Anian.   
\p
\v 20 And the sons of Ephraim; Sothalath, and Bedad his son, and Tahath his son, Elada his son, Saath his son,  
\v 21 and Zabad his son, Sothele his son, and Azer, and Elead: and the men of Geth who were born in the land slew them, because they went down to take their cattle.  
\v 22 And their father Ephraim mourned many days, and his brothers came to comfort him.  
\v 23 And he went in to his wife, and she conceived, and bore a son, and he called his name Beria, because, \add he said\add*, He was afflicted in my house.  
\v 24 And his daughter \add was\add* Saraa, and he was among them who were left, and he built Beth-horon the upper and the lower. And the descendants of Ozan \add were\add* Seera,  
\v 25 and Raphe his son, Saraph and Thalees his sons, Thaen his son.  
\v 26 To Laadan his son \add was born his\add* son Amiud, his son Helisamai, \add his\add* son  
\v 27 Nun, \add his\add* son Jesue, \add these were\add* his sons.   
\p
\v 28 And their possession and their dwelling \add were\add* Bethel and her towns, to the east Noaran, westward Gezer and her towns, and Shechem and her towns, as far as Gaza and her towns.  
\v 29 And as far as the borders of the sons of Manasseh, Bæthsaan and her towns, Thanach and her towns, Mageddo and her towns, Dor and her towns. In this the children of Joseph the son of Israel dwelt.   
\p
\v 30 The sons of Aser; Imnah, and Suia, and Isui, and Beria, and Sore their sister.  
\v 31 And the sons of Beria; Chaber, and Malchiel; he \add was\add* the father of Berthaith.  
\v 32 And Chaber begot Japhlet, and Shamir, and Chothan, and Shagee their sister.  
\v 33 And the sons of Japhlet; Phasec, and Bamael, and Asith: these \add are\add* the sons of Japhlet.  
\v 34 And the sons of Semmer; Achir, and Rooga, and Jaba, and Aram.  
\v 35 And the sons of Elam his brother; Sopha, and Imana, and Selles, and Amal.  
\v 36 The sons of Sopha; Sue, and Arnaphar, and Suda, and Barin, and Imran,  
\v 37 and Bashan, and Oa, and Sama, and Salisa, and Jethra, and Beëra.  
\v 38 And the sons of Jeths, Jephina, and Phaspha, and Ara.  
\v 39 And the sons of Ola; Erech, Hanniel, and Rasia.   
\p
\v 40 All these \add were\add* the sons of Aser, all heads of families, choice, mighty men, chief leaders: their number for battle array—their number \add was\add* twenty-six thousand men.   
\c 8  
\p
\v 1 Now Benjamin begot Bela his first-born, and Ashbel his second \add son\add*, Aara the third, Noa the fourth,  
\v 2 and Rapha the fifth.  
\v 3 And the sons of Bela were, Adir, and Gera, and Abiud,  
\v 4 and Abessue, and Noama, and Ahijah,  
\v 5 and Gera, and Sephupham, and Uram.  
\v 6 These \add were\add* the sons of Ohad: these are the heads of families to them who dwell in Gabee, and they removed them to Machanathi:  
\v 7 and Nooma, and Ahijah and Gera, he removed them, and he begot Ezer, and Jachicho.   
\p
\v 8 And Saarin begot \add children\add* in the plain of Moab, after that he had sent away Osin and Baada his wives.   
\p
\v 9 And he begot of his wife Ada, Jolab, and Sebia, and Misa, and Melchas,  
\v 10 and Jebus, and Zabia, and Marma: these \add were\add* heads of families.  
\v 11 And of Osin he begot Abitol, and Alphaal.  
\v 12 And the sons of Alphaal; Obed, Misaal, Semmer: he built Ona, and Lod, and its towns:  
\v 13 and Beria, and Sama; these \add were\add* heads of families among the dwellers in Elam, and they drove out the inhabitants of Geth.  
\v 14 And his brothers \add were\add* Sosec, and Arimoth,  
\v 15 and Zebadiah, and Ored, and Eder,  
\v 16 and Michael, and Jespha, and Joda, the sons of Beria:  
\v 17 and Zebadiah, and Meshullam, and Azaki, and Abar,  
\v 18 and Isamari, and Jexlias, and Jobab, the sons of Elphaal:  
\v 19 and Jakim, and Zachri, and Zabdi,  
\v 20 and Eliehoenai, and Salathi,  
\v 21 and Elieli, and Adaia, and Baraia, and Samarath, sons of Samaith:  
\v 22 and Jesphan, and Obed, and Eliel,  
\v 23 and Abdon, and Zichri, and Anan,  
\v 24 and Hananiah, and Omri, and Elam, \add and\add* Anathoth,  
\v 25 and Jathin, and Jephadias, and Penuel, the sons of Sosec:  
\v 26 and Samsari, and Saarias, and Gotholia,  
\v 27 and Jarasia, and Eria, and Zichri, son of Jeroham.  
\v 28 These \add were\add* heads of families, chiefs according to their generations: these dwelt in Jerusalem.   
\p
\v 29 And the father of Gibeon dwelt in Gibeon; and his wife's name was Moacha.  
\v 30 And her first-born son was Abdon, and Shur, and Kish, and Baal, and Nadab, and Ner,  
\v 31 and Gedur and his brother, and Zacchur, and Makeloth.  
\v 32 And Makeloth begot Samaa: for these dwelt in Jerusalem in the presence of their brothers with their brothers.  
\v 33 And Ner begot Kish, and Kish begot Saul, and Saul begot Jonathan, and Melchisue, and Aminadab, and Asabal.  
\v 34 And the son of Jonathan \add was\add* Meribaal; and Meribaal begot Micha.  
\v 35 And the sons of Micha; Phithon, and Melach, and Tharach, and Ahaz.  
\v 36 And Ahaz begot Jada, and Jada begot Salæmath, and Asmoth, and Zimri; and Zimri begot Mæsa;  
\v 37 and Mæsa begot Baanah: Rhaphæa, \add was\add* his son, Elasa his son, Esel his son.   
\p
\v 38 And Esel \add had\add* six sons, and these \add were\add* their names; Azrikam his first-born, and Ishmael, and Seraiah, and Obadiah, and Anan, and Asa: all these \add were\add* the sons of Esel.  
\v 39 And the sons of Asel his brother; Elam his first-born, and Jas the second, and Eliphalet the third.  
\v 40 And the sons of Elam were mighty men, bending the bow, and multiplying sons and grandsons, a hundred \add and\add* fifty. All these \add were\add* of the sons of Benjamin.   
\c 9  
\p
\v 1 And \add this is\add* all Israel, \add even\add* their enrolment: and these \add are\add* written down in the book of the kings of Israel and Judah, with the \add names of them\add* that were carried away to Babylon for their transgressions.  
\v 2 And they who dwelt before in their possessions in the cities of Israel, the priests, the Levites, and the appointed ones.   
\p
\v 3 And there dwelt in Jerusalem Shammah of the children of Judah, and of the children of Benjamin, and of the children of Ephraim, and Manasseh.  
\v 4 And Gnothi, and the son of Samiud, the son of Amri, the son of Ambraim, the son of Buni, son of the sons of Phares, the son of Judah.  
\v 5 And of the Selonites; Asaia his first-born, and his sons.  
\v 6 Of the sons of Zerah; Jehiel, and their brothers, six hundred and ninety.   
\p
\v 7 And of the sons of Benjamin; Salom, son of Meshullam, son of Odouia, son of Asinu.  
\v 8 And Jemnaa son of Jeroboam, and Elo: these \add are\add* the sons of Uzza the son of Machir: and Meshullam, son of Shephatiah, son of Reuel, son of Jemnai;  
\v 9 and their brothers according to their generations, nine hundred and fifty-six, all the men \add were\add* heads of families according to the houses of their fathers.   
\p
\v 10 And of the priests; Jodaë, and Jehoiarib, and Jachin,  
\v 11 and Azariah the son of Hilkiah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the son of Maraïoth, the son of Ahitub, the ruler of the house of God;  
\v 12 and Adaia son of Iraam, son of Phascor, son of Malchijah, and Maasaia son of Adiel, son of Ezira, son of Meshullam, son of Maselmoth, son of Immer;  
\v 13 and their brothers, chiefs of their families, a thousand seven hundred and sixty, mighty \add men\add* for the work of the ministration of the house of God.   
\p
\v 14 And of the Levites; Shemaiah son of Asob, son of Azrikam, son of Asabia, of the sons of Merari.  
\v 15 And Bacbacar, and Arah, and Galaal, and Mattaniah son of Micha, son of Zichri, son of Asaph;  
\v 16 and Obadiah, son of Samia, son of Galaal, son of Jeduthun, and Berechiah son of Ossa, son of Elkanah—who dwelt in the villages of the Notephatites.  
\v 17 The door-keepers; Salom, Acum, Talmon, and Diman, and their brothers; Salom \add was\add* the chief;  
\v 18 and \add he waited\add* hitherto in the king's gate eastward: these \add are\add* the gates of the companies of the sons of Levi.  
\v 19 And Shallum the son of Korah, the son of Abiasaph, the son of Korah, and his brothers belonging to the house of his father, the Corites \add were\add* over the works of the service, keeping the watches of the tabernacle, and their fathers over the camp of the Lord, keeping the entrance.   
\p
\v 20 And Phinehas son of Eleazar was head over them before the Lord, and these \add were\add* with him.  
\v 21 Zacharias the son of Mosollami \add was\add* keeper of the door of the tabernacle of witness.  
\v 22 All the chosen porters in the gates \add were\add* two hundred and twelve, these \add were\add* in their courts, \add this was\add* their distribution: these David and Samuel the seer established in their charge.  
\v 23 And these and their sons \add were\add* over the gates in the house of the Lord, and in the house of the tabernacle, to keep watch.  
\v 24 The gates were toward the four winds, eastward, westward, northward, southward.  
\v 25 And their brothers \add were\add* in their courts, to enter in weekly from time to time with these.  
\v 26 For four strong \add men\add* have the charge of the gates; and the Levites were over the chambers, and they keep watch over the treasures of the house of God.  
\v 27 For the charge \add was\add* upon them, and these \add were\add* charged with the keys to open the doors of the temple every morning.   
\p
\v 28 And \add Shammah\add* of them \add were appointed\add* over the vessels of service, that they should carry them in by number, and carry them out by number.  
\v 29 And \add Shammah\add* of them \add were\add* appointed over the furniture, and over all the holy vessels, and over the fine flour, the wine, the oil, the frankincense, and the spices.  
\v 30 And Shammah of the priests were makers of the ointment, and \add appointed to prepare\add* the spices.  
\v 31 And Mattithiah of the Levites, (he \add was\add* the first-born of Salom the Corite,) \add was set\add* in charge over the sacrifices of meat-offering of the pan belonging to the high priest.  
\v 32 And Benaiah the Caathite, from among their brothers, \add was set\add* over the shewbread, to prepare it every sabbath.  
\v 33 And these \add were\add* the singers, heads of families of the Levites, \add to whom were\add* established daily courses, for they were employed in the services day and night.  
\v 34 These \add were\add* the heads of the families of the Levites according to their generations; these chiefs dwelt in Jerusalem.   
\p
\v 35 And Jeël the father of Gibeon dwelt in Gibeon; and his wife's name \add was\add* Moöcha.  
\v 36 And his first-born son \add was\add* Abdon, and \add he had\add* Shur, and Kish, and Baal, and Ner, and Nadab,  
\v 37 and Gedur and \add his\add* brother, and Zacchur, and Makeloth.  
\v 38 And Makeloth begot Samaa: and these dwelt in the midst of their brothers in Jerusalem, \add even\add* in the midst of their brothers.   
\p
\v 39 And Ner begot Kish, and Kish begot Saul, and Saul begot Jonathan, and Melchisue, and Aminadab, and Asabal.  
\v 40 And the son of Jonathan \add was\add* Meribaal: and Meribaal begot Micha.  
\v 41 And the sons of Micha \add were\add* Phithon and Malach, and Tharach.  
\v 42 And Ahaz begot Jada: and Jada begot Galems, and Gazmoth, and Zimri; and Zimri begot Massa.  
\v 43 And Massa begot Baanah, and Rhaphaïa \add was\add* his son, Elasa his son, Esel his son.  
\v 44 And Esel had six sons, and these \add were\add* their names; Esricam his first-born, and Ishmael, and Seraiah, and Obadiah, and Anan, and Asa: these \add were\add* the sons of Esel.   
\c 10  
\p
\v 1 Now the Philistines warred against Israel; and they fled from before the Philistines, and fell down slain in mount Gelbue.  
\v 2 And the Philistines pursued after Saul, and after his sons; and the Philistines struck Jonathan, and Aminadab, and Melchisue, sons of Saul.  
\v 3 And the battle prevailed against Saul, and the archers hit him with bows and arrows, and they were wounded of the bows.  
\v 4 And Saul said to his armour-bearer, Draw your sword, and pierce me through with it, lest these uncircumcised come and mock me. But his armour-bearer would not, for he was greatly afraid: so Saul took a sword, and fell upon it.  
\v 5 And his armour-bearer saw that Saul was dead, and he also fell upon his sword.  
\v 6 So Saul died, and his three sons on that day, and all his family died at the Shuham time.  
\v 7 And all the men of Israel that were in the valley saw that Israel fled, and that Saul and his sons were dead, and they left their cities, and fled: and the Philistines came and dwelt in them.   
\p
\v 8 And it came to pass on the next \add day\add* that the Philistines came to strip the slain, and they found Saul and his sons fallen on mount Gelbue.  
\v 9 And they stripped him, and took his head, and his armour, and sent them into the land of the Philistines round about, to proclaim the glad tidings to their idols, and to the people.  
\v 10 And they put their armour in the house of their god, and they put his head in the house of Dagon.   
\p
\v 11 And all the dwellers in Gilead heard of all that the Philistines had done to Saul and to Israel.  
\v 12 And all the mighty men rose up from Gilead, and they took the body of Saul, and the bodies of his sons, and brought them to Jabez, and buried their bones under the oak in Jabez, and fasted seven days.  
\v 13 So Saul died for his transgressions, wherein he transgressed against God, against the word of the Lord, forasmuch as he kept \add it\add* not, because Saul inquired of a wizard to seek \add counsel\add*, and Samuel the prophet answered him:  
\v 14 and he sought not the Lord: so he slew him, and turned the kingdom to David the son of Jesse.   
\c 11  
\p
\v 1 And all Israel came to David in Hebron, saying, Behold, we \add are\add* your bones and your flesh.  
\v 2 And heretofore when Saul was king, you wast He who led Israel in and out, and the Lord of Israel said to you, You shall feed my people Israel, and you shall be for a ruler over Israel.  
\v 3 And all the elders of Israel came to the king to Hebron; and king David made a covenant with them in Hebron before the Lord: and they anointed David to be king over Israel, according to the word of the Lord by Samuel.   
\p
\v 4 And the king and his men went to Jerusalem, this \add is\add* Jebus; and there the Jebusites the inhabitants of the land said to David,  
\v 5 You shall not enter in here. But he took the strong hold of Zion: this \add is\add* the city of David.  
\v 6 And David said, Whoever first smites the Jebusite, even he shall be chief and captain. And Joab the son of Zeruiah went up first, and became chief.  
\v 7 And David dwelt in the strong hold; therefore he called it the city of David.  
\v 8 And he fortified the city round about.  
\v 9 And David continued to increase, and the Lord Almighty \add was\add* with him.  
\v 10 And these \add are\add* the chiefs of the mighty men, whom David had, who strengthened \add themselves\add* with him in his kingdom, with all Israel, to make him king, according to the word of the Lord concerning Israel.   
\p
\v 11 And this \add is\add* the list of the mighty \add men\add* of David; Jashobeam, son of Hachmoni, first of the thirty: he drew his sword once against three hundred whom he slew at one time.  
\v 12 And after him Eleazar son of Dodo, the Ahohite: he was among the three mighty men.  
\v 13 He was with David in Pas-dammim, and the Philistines were gathered there to battle, and \add there was\add* a portion of the field full of barley; and the people fled before the Philistines.  
\v 14 And he stood in the midst of the portion, and rescued it, and struck the Philistines; and the Lord worked a great deliverance.   
\p
\v 15 And three of the thirty chiefs went down to the rock to David, to the cave of Adullam, and the camp of the Philistines \add was\add* in the giants' valley.  
\v 16 And David \add was\add* then in the hold, and the garrison of the Philistines \add was\add* then in Bethlehem.  
\v 17 And David longed, and said, Who will give me water to drink of the well of Bethlehem, that is in the gate?  
\v 18 And the three broke through the camp of the Philistines, and they drew water out of the well that was in Bethlehem, which was in the gate, and they took it, and came to David: but David would not drink it, and poured it out to the Lord, and said,  
\v 19 God forbid that I should do this thing: shall I drink the blood of these men with their lives? for with \add the peril of\add* their lives they brought it. So he would not drink it. These things did the three mighty \add men\add*.   
\p
\v 20 And Abishai the brother of Joab, he was chief of three: he drew his sword against three hundred slain at one time, and he had a name among the \add second\add* three.  
\v 21 He was more famous than the two \add others\add* of the three, and he was chief \add over\add* them; yet he reached not to the \add first\add* three.   
\p
\v 22 And Benaiah the son of Jodae was the son of a mighty man: many \add were\add* his acts for Kabzeel: he struck two lion-like men of Moab, and he went down and struck a lion in a pit on a snowy day.  
\v 23 And he struck an Egyptian, a wonderful man five cubits \add high\add*; and in the hand of the Egyptian \add there was\add* a spear like a weavers' beam; and Benaiah went down to him with a staff, and took the spear out of the Egyptian's hand, and slew him with his own spear.  
\v 24 These things did Benaiah son of Jodae, and his name \add was\add* among the three mighties.  
\v 25 He was distinguished beyond the thirty, yet he reached not to the \add first\add* three: and David set him over his family.   
\p
\v 26 And the mighty \add men\add* of the forces \add were\add*, Asahel the brother of Joab, Elhanan the son of Dodo of Bethlehem,  
\v 27 Shammoth the Harorite, Helez the Pelonite,  
\v 28 Ira the son of Ikkesh the Tekoite, Abiezer the Anathothite,  
\v 29 Sibbecai the Hushathite, Eli the Ahohite,  
\v 30 Maharai the Netophathite, Heled the son of Baanah the Netophathite,  
\v 31 Ithai the son of Ribai of the hill of Benjamin, Benaiah the Pirathonite,  
\v 32 Uri of Nachali Gaas, Abiel the Arbathite,  
\v 33 Azmavs the Baharumite, Eliahba the Shaalbonite,  
\v 34 the son of Asam the Gizonite, Jonathan the son of Shagee the Hararite,  
\v 35 Ahiam the son of Sachar the Hararite, Eliphal the son of Ur  
\v 36 the Mecherathite, Ahijah the Phellonite,  
\v 37 Hezro the Carmelite, Naarai the son of Ezbai,  
\v 38 Joel the son of Nathan, Mibhar son of Hagri,  
\v 39 Zelek the son of Ammonite, Nahor the Beerothite, armour-bearer to the son of Zeruiah,  
\v 40 Ira the Ithrite, Gaber the Ithrite,  
\v 41 Uriah the Hittite, Zabad son of Ahlai,  
\v 42 Adina son of Shiza, a chief of Reuben, and thirty with him,  
\v 43 Anan the son of Moöcha, and Josaphat the Mithnite,  
\v 44 Ozia the Ashterathite, Shama and Jeiel sons of Hotham the Hararite,  
\v 45 Jediel the son of Shimri, and Joha his brother the Tizite,  
\v 46 Eliel the Mahavite, and Jeribai, and Josia his son, Elnaam, and Ithmah the Moabite,  
\v 47 Eliel, and Obed, and Jaasiel of Mezobaite.   
\c 12  
\p
\v 1 And these \add are\add* they who came to Ziklag, when he yet kept himself close because of Saul the son of Kish; and these \add were\add* among the mighty, aiding \add him\add* in war,  
\v 2 and \add using\add* the bow with the right hand and with the left, and slingers with stones, and \add shooters\add* with bows. Of the brothers of Saul of Benjamin,  
\v 3 the chief \add was\add* Achiezer, and Joash son of Shemaah the Gibeathite, and Joel and Pelet, sons of Asmoth, and Berchia, and Jeul of Anathoth,  
\v 4 and Samaias the Gibeonite a mighty man among the thirty, and over the thirty;  
\v 5 \add and\add* Jeremiah, and Jahaziel, and Joanan, and Jozabath of Gederathite,  
\v 6 Eluzai and Jerimoth, and Bealiah, and Shemariah, and Saphatias of Haruphite,  
\v 7 Elkanah, and Isshiah, and Azarel, and Joezer, and Jashobeam, and the Corites,  
\v 8 and Joelah and Zebadiah, sons of Jeroham, and the \add men\add* of Gedor.   
\p
\v 9 And from Gad these separated themselves to David from the wilderness, strong mighty men of war, bearing shields and spears, and their faces \add were as\add* the face of a lion, and they were nimble as roes upon the mountains in speed.  
\v 10 Ezer the chief, Obadiah the second, Eliab the third,  
\v 11 Mishmannah the fourth, Jeremiah the fifth,  
\v 12 Attai the sixth, Eliab the seventh,  
\v 13 Joanan the eighth, Eleazer the ninth,  
\v 14 Jeremiah the tenth, Machbanai the eleventh.  
\v 15 These \add were\add* chiefs of the army of the sons of Gad, the least one commander of a hundred, and the greatest one of a thousand.  
\v 16 These \add are\add* the \add men\add* that crossed over Jordan in the first month, and it had overflowed all its banks; and they drove out all the inhabitants of the valleys, from the east to the west.   
\p
\v 17 And there came \add Shammah\add* of the sons of Benjamin and Judah to the assistance of David.  
\v 18 And David went out to meet them, and said to them, If you are come peaceably to me, let my heart be at peace with you: but if \add you are come\add* to betray me to my enemies unfaithfully, the God of your fathers look upon it, and reprove it.  
\v 19 And the Spirit came upon Amasai, a captain of the thirty, and he said, Go, David, son of Jesse, you and your people, peace, peace be to you, and peace to your helpers, for your God has helped you. And David received them, and made them captains of the forces.   
\p
\v 20 And \add Shammah\add* came to David from Manasseh, when the Philistines came against Saul to war: and he helped them not, because the captains of the Philistines took counsel, saying, With the heads of those men will he return to his master Saul.  
\v 21 When David was going to Ziklag, there came to him of Manasseh, Adnah and Jozabath, and Jediael, and Michael, and Jozabad, and Elihu, and Zillethai: \add these\add* are the captains of thousands of Manasseh.  
\v 22 And they fought on the side of David against a troop, for they \add were\add* all men of might; and they were commanders in the army, \add because\add* of \add their\add* might.  
\v 23 For daily men came to David, \add till they amounted\add* to a great force, as the force of God.   
\p
\v 24 And these \add are\add* the names of the commanders of the army, who came to David to Hebron, to turn the kingdom of Saul to him according to the word of the Lord.  
\v 25 The sons of Judah, bearing shields and spears, six thousand and eight hundred mighty in war.  
\v 26 Of the sons of Simeon mighty for battle, seven thousand and a hundred.  
\v 27 Of the sons of Levi, four thousand and six hundred.  
\v 28 And Jehoiada the chief \add of the family\add* of Aaron, and with him three thousand and seven hundred.  
\v 29 And Zadok, a young \add man\add* mighty in strength, and \add there were\add* twenty-two leaders of his father's house.  
\v 30 And of the sons of Benjamin, the brothers of Saul, three thousand: and still the greater part of them kept the guard of the house of Saul.  
\v 31 And of the sons of Ephraim, twenty thousand and eight hundred mighty men, famous in the houses of their fathers.  
\v 32 And of the half-tribe of Manasseh, eighteen thousand, even \add those\add* who were named by name, to make David king.  
\v 33 And of the sons of Issachar having wisdom with regard to the times, knowing what Israel should do, two hundred; and all their brothers with them.   
\p
\v 34 And of Zebulun they who went out to battle, with all weapons of war, \add were\add* fifty thousand to help David, not weak-handed.  
\v 35 And of Naphtali a thousand captains, and with them \add men\add* with shields and spears, thirty-seven thousand.  
\v 36 And of the Danites \add men\add* ready for war twenty-eight thousand and eight hundred.  
\v 37 And of Aser, they who went out to give aid in war, forty thousand.  
\v 38 And from the country beyond Jordan, from Reuben, and the Gadites, and from the half-tribe of Manasseh, a hundred and twenty thousand, with all weapons of war.   
\p
\v 39 All these \add were\add* men of war, setting \add the army\add* in battle array, with a peaceful mind \add towards him\add*, and they came to Hebron to make David king over all Israel: and the rest of Israel \add were of\add* one mind to make David king.  
\v 40 And they were there three days eating and drinking, for their brothers \add had\add* made preparations.  
\v 41 And their neighbours, as far as Issachar and Zebulun and Naphtali, brought to them upon camels, and asses, and mules, and upon calves, victuals, meal, cakes of figs, raisins, wine, and oil, calves and sheep abundantly: for \add there was\add* joy in Israel.   
\c 13  
\p
\v 1 And David took counsel with the captains of thousands and captains of hundreds, \add even with\add* every commander.  
\v 2 And David said to the whole congregation of Israel, If it \add seem\add* good to you, and it should be prospered by the Lord our God, let us send to our brothers that are left in all the land of Israel, and let the priests the Levites who are with them in the cities of their possession \add come\add*, and let them be gathered to us.  
\v 3 And let us bring over to us the ark of our God; for men have not inquired \add at\add* it since the days of Saul.  
\v 4 And all the congregation said that they would do thus; for the saying was right in the eyes of all the people.   
\p
\v 5 So David assembled all Israel, from the borders of Egypt even to the entering in of Hammath, to bring in the ark of God from the city of Jarim.  
\v 6 And David brought it up: and all Israel went up to the city of David, which belonged to Judah, to bring up from there the ark of the Lord God who sits between the cherubim, whose name is called \add on it\add*.  
\v 7 And they set the ark of God on a new waggon \add brought\add* out of the house of Aminadab: and Azzan and his brothers drove the waggon.   
\p
\v 8 And David and all Israel \add were\add* playing before the Lord with all their might, and \add that\add* together with singers, and with harps, and with lutes, with timbrels, and with cymbals, and with trumpets.  
\v 9 And they came as far as the threshing-floor: and Azzan put forth his hand to hold the ark, because the bullock moved it from \add its place\add*.  
\v 10 And the Lord was very angry with Azzan, and struck him there, because of his stretching forth his hand upon the ark: and he died there before God.  
\v 11 And David was dispirited, because the Lord \add had\add* made a breach on Azzan: and he called that place the Breach of Azzan until this day.  
\v 12 And David feared God that day, saying, How shall I bring the ark of God in to myself?  
\v 13 So David brought not the ark home to himself into the city of David, but he turned it aside into the house of Abeddara the Gethite.   
\p
\v 14 And the ark of God abode in the house of Abeddara three months: and God blessed Abeddara and all that he had.   
\c 14  
\p
\v 1 And Chiram king of Tyre sent messengers to David, and cedar timbers, and masons, and carpenters, to build a house for him.  
\v 2 And David knew that the Lord \add had\add* designed him to be king over Israel; because his kingdom was highly exalted, on account of his people Israel.   
\p
\v 3 And David took more wives in Jerusalem: and there were born to David more sons and daughters.  
\v 4 And these \add are\add* the names of those that were born, who were \add born\add* to him in Jerusalem; Samaa, Shobab, Nathan, and Solomon,  
\v 5 and Baar, and Elisa, and Eliphelet,  
\v 6 and Nageth, and Naphath, and Japhia,  
\v 7 and Elisamae, and Eliade, and Eliphelet.   
\p
\v 8 And the Philistines heard that David was anointed king over all Israel: and all the Philistines went up to seek David; and David heard \add it\add*, and went out to meet them.  
\v 9 And the Philistines came and assembled together in the giants' valley.  
\v 10 And David inquired of God, saying, Shall I go up against the Philistines? and will you deliver them into my hand? And the Lord said to him, Go up, and I will deliver them into your hands.  
\v 11 And he went up to Baal Pharasin, and David struck them there; and David said, God has broken through enemies by my hand like a breach of water: therefore he called the name of that place, the Breach of Pharasin.  
\v 12 And the Philistines left their gods there; and David gave orders to burn them with fire.   
\p
\v 13 And the Philistines once more assembled themselves in the giants' valley.  
\v 14 And David inquired of God again; and God said to him, You shall not go after them; turn away from them, and you shall come upon them near the pear trees.  
\v 15 And it shall be, when you shall hear the sound of their tumult in the tops of the pear trees, then you shall go into the battle: for God has gone out before you to smite the army of the Philistines.  
\v 16 And he did as God commanded him: and he struck the army of the Philistines from Gibeon to Gazera.  
\v 17 And the name of David was \add famous\add* in all the land; and the Lord put the terror of him on all the nations.   
\c 15  
\p
\v 1 And \add David\add* made for himself houses in the city of David, and he prepared a place for the ark of God, and made a tent for it.  
\v 2 Then said David, It is not \add lawful for any\add* to bear the ark of God, but the Levites; for the Lord has chosen them to bear the ark of the Lord, and to minister to him for ever.   
\p
\v 3 And David assembled all Israel at Jerusalem, to bring up the ark of the Lord to the place which he \add had\add* prepared for it.  
\v 4 And David gathered together the sons of Aaron the Levites.  
\v 5 Of the sons of Kohath; \add there was\add* Uriel the chief, and his brothers, a hundred and twenty.  
\v 6 Of the sons of Merari; Asaia the chief, and his brothers, two hundred and twenty.  
\v 7 Of the sons of Gershon; Joel the chief, and his brothers, a hundred and thirty.  
\v 8 Of the sons of Elisaphat; Semei the chief, and his brothers, two hundred.  
\v 9 Of the sons of Chebrom; Eliel the chief, and his brothers eighty.  
\v 10 Of the sons of Oziel; Aminadab the chief, and his brothers a hundred and twelve.   
\p
\v 11 And David called Zadok and Abiathar the priests, and the Levites, Uriel, Asaia, and Joel, and Semaia, and Eliel, and Aminadab,  
\v 12 and said to them, You \add are\add* the heads of the families of the Levites: sanctify yourselves, you and your brothers, and you shall carry up the ark of the God of Israel, \add to the place\add* which I have prepared for it.  
\v 13 For because you were not \add ready\add* at the first, our God made a breach upon us, because we sought him not according to the ordinance.  
\v 14 So the priests and the Levites sanctified themselves, to bring up the ark of the God of Israel.  
\v 15 And the sons of the Levites took the ark of God, (as Moses commanded by the word of God according to the scripture) upon their shoulders with staves.   
\p
\v 16 And David said to the chiefs of the Levites, Set your brothers the singers with musical instruments, lutes, harps, and cymbals, to sound aloud with a voice of joy.  
\v 17 So the Levites appointed Heman the son of Joel; Asaph the son of Barachias \add was one\add* of his brothers; and Æthan the son of Kisæus was of the sons of Merari their brothers;  
\v 18 and with them their brothers of the second rank, Zacharias, and Oziel, and Semiramoth, and Jeiel, and Elioel, and Eliab, and Benaiah, and Maasaia, and Matthathia, and Eliphena, and Makellia, and Obed-edom, and Jeiel, and Ozias, the porters.  
\v 19 And the singers, Heman, Asaph, and Æthan, with brazen cymbals to make \add a sound\add* to be heard.  
\v 20 Zacharias, and Oziel, Semiramoth, Jeiel, Oni, Eliab, Maasæas, Benaiah, with lutes, on alæmoth.  
\v 21 And Mattathias, and Eliphalu, and Makenia, and Obed-edom, and Jeiel, and Ozias, with harps of Amasenith, to make a loud noise.   
\p
\v 22 And Chenaniah chief of the Levites \add was\add* master of the bands, because he was skilful.  
\v 23 And Berechiah and Elcana \add were\add* door-keepers of the ark.  
\v 24 And Somnia, and Josaphat, and Nethanel, and Amasai, and Zechariah, and Banæa, and Eliezer, the priests, were sounding with trumpets before the ark of God: and Obed-edom and Jeia \add were\add* door-keepers of the ark of God.   
\p
\v 25 So David, and the elders of Israel, and the captains of thousands, went to bring up the ark of the covenant from the house of Obed-edom with gladness.  
\v 26 And it came to pass when God strengthened the Levites bearing the ark of the covenant of the Lord, that they sacrificed seven calves and seven rams.  
\v 27 And David \add was\add* girt with a fine linen robe, and all the Levites \add who were\add* bearing the ark of the covenant of the Lord, and the singers, and Chonenias the master of the band of singers; also upon David \add there was\add* a robe of fine linen.  
\v 28 And all Israel brought up the ark of the covenant of the Lord with shouting, and with the sound of a horn, and with trumpets, and with cymbals, playing loudly on lutes and harps.  
\v 29 And the ark of the covenant of the Lord arrived, and came to the city of David; and Melchol the daughter of Saul looked down through the window, and saw king David dancing and playing: and she despised him in her heart.   
\c 16  
\p
\v 1 So they brought in the ark of God, and set it in the midst of the tabernacle which David pitched for it; and they offered whole-burnt-offerings and peace-offerings before God.  
\v 2 And David finished offering up whole-burnt-offerings and peace-offerings, and blessed the people in the name of the Lord.  
\v 3 And he divided to every man of Israel (both men and women), to \add every\add* man one baker's loaf, and a cake.  
\v 4 And he appointed before the ark of the covenant of the Lord, Levites to minister \add and\add* lift up the voice, and to give thanks and praise the Lord God of Israel:  
\v 5 Asaph \add was\add* the chief, and next to him Zacharias, Jeiel, Semiramoth, and Jeiel, Mattathias, Eliab, and Benaiah, and Obed-edom: and Jeiel sounding with musical instruments, lutes \add and\add* harps, and Asaph with cymbals:  
\v 6 and Benaiah and Oziel the priests \add sounding\add* continually with trumpets before the ark of the covenant of God in that day.   
\p
\v 7 Then David first gave orders to praise the Lord by the hand of Asaph and his brothers.   
\p
\v 8 Song. Give thanks to the Lord, call upon him by his name, make known his designs among the people.  
\v 9 Sing \add songs\add* to him, and sing hymns to him, relate to all \add people\add* his wonderful deeds, which the Lord has worked.  
\v 10 Praise his holy name, the heart that seeks his pleasure shall rejoice.  
\v 11 Seek the Lord and be strong, seek his face continually.  
\v 12 Remember his wonderful works which he has worked, his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth;  
\v 13 \add you\add* seed of Israel his servants, \add you\add* seed of Jacob his chosen ones.  
\v 14 He \add is\add* the Lord our God; his judgments \add are\add* in all the earth.  
\v 15 Let us remember his covenant for ever, his word which he commanded to a thousand generations,  
\v 16 which he covenanted with Abraham, and his oath \add sworn\add* to Isaac.  
\v 17 He confirmed it to Jacob for an ordinance, to Israel \add as\add* an everlasting covenant,  
\v 18 saying, To you will I give the land of Canaan, the line of your inheritance:  
\v 19 when they were few in number, when they were but little, and dwelt as strangers in it;  
\v 20 and went from nation to nation, and from one kingdom to another people.  
\v 21 He suffered not a man to oppress them, and he reproved kings for their sakes,  
\v 22 saying, Touch not my anointed ones, and deal not wrongfully with my prophets.   
\p
\v 23 Sing you to the Lord, all the earth; proclaim his salvation from day to day.  
\v 23a Declare among the nations his glory, his wondrous deeds among all peoples.  
\v 25 For the Lord \add is\add* great, and greatly to be praised: he \add is\add* to be feared above all gods.  
\v 26 For all the gods of the nations \add are\add* idols; but our God made the heavens.  
\v 27 Glory and praise \add are\add* in his presence; strength and rejoicing \add are\add* in his place.  
\v 28 Give to the Lord, you families of the nations, give to the Lord glory and strength.  
\v 29 Give to the Lord the glory \add belonging\add* to his name: take gifts and offer \add them\add* before him; and worship the Lord in his holy courts.  
\v 30 Let the whole earth fear before him; let the earth be established, and not be moved.  
\v 31 Let the heavens rejoice, and let the earth exult; and let them say among the nations, The Lord reigns.  
\v 32 The sea with its fulness shall resound and the tree of the field, and all things in it.  
\v 33 Then shall the trees of the wood rejoice before the Lord, for he is come to judge the earth.  
\v 34 Give thanks to the Lord, for \add it is\add* good, for his mercy \add is\add* for ever.  
\v 35 And say you, Save us, O God of our salvation, and gather us, and rescue us from among the heathen, that we may praise your holy name, and glory in your praises.  
\v 36 Blessed \add be\add* the Lord God of Israel from everlasting and to everlasting:  
\p And all the people shall say, Amen. So they praised the Lord.   
\p
\v 37 And they left there Asaph and his brothers before the ark of the covenant of the Lord, to minister before the ark continually, according to the service of each day: from day to day.  
\v 38 And Obed-edom and his brothers \add were\add* sixty and eight; and Obed-edom the son of Jeduthun, and Hosah, \add were\add* to be door-keepers.  
\v 39 And \add they appointed\add* Zadok the priest, and his brothers the priests, before the tabernacle of the Lord in the high place in Gibeon,  
\v 40 to offer up whole-burnt-offerings to the Lord on the altar of whole-burnt-offerings continually morning and evening, and according to all things written in the law of the Lord, which he commanded the children of Israel by Moses the servant of God.  
\v 41 And with him \add were\add* Heman and Jeduthun, and the rest chosen out by name to praise the Lord, for his mercy \add endures\add* for ever.  
\v 42 And with them \add there were\add* trumpets and cymbals to sound aloud, and musical instruments for the songs of God: and the sons of Jeduthun \add were\add* at the gate.   
\p
\v 43 And all the people went every one to his home: and David returned to bless his house.   
\c 17  
\p
\v 1 And it came to pass as David dwelt in his house, that David said to Nathan the prophet, Behold, I dwell in a house of cedar, but the ark of the covenant of the Lord \add is\add* under \add curtains\add* of skins.   
\p
\v 2 And Nathan said to David, Do all that is in your heart; for God \add is\add* with you.   
\p
\v 3 And it came to pass in that night, that the word of the Lord came to Nathan, \add saying\add*,  
\v 4 Go and say to David my servant, Thus said the Lord, You shall not build me a house for me to dwell in it.  
\v 5 For I have not dwelt in a house from the day that I brought up Israel until this day, but I have been in a tabernacle and a tent,  
\v 6 in all places through which I have gone with all Israel: did I ever speak to \add any\add* one tribe of Israel whom I commanded to feed my people, saying, \add Why is it\add* that you have not built me a house of cedar?  
\v 7 And now thus shall you say to my servant David, Thus saith the Lord Almighty, I took you from the sheepfold, from following the flocks, to be a ruler over my people Israel:  
\v 8 and I was with you in all places where you went, and I destroyed all yours enemies from before you, and I made for you a name according to the name of the great ones that are upon the earth.  
\v 9 And I will appoint a place for my people Israel, and I will plant him, and he shall dwell by himself, and shall no longer be anxious; and the son of iniquity shall no longer afflict him, as at the beginning,  
\v 10 and from the days when I appointed judges over my people Israel. Also I have humbled all yours enemies, and I will increase you, and the Lord will build you a house.  
\v 11 And it shall come to pass when your days shall be fulfilled, and you shall sleep with your fathers, that I will raise up your seed after you, which shall be of your bowels, and I will establish his kingdom.  
\v 12 He shall build me a house, and I will set up his throne for ever.  
\v 13 I will be to him a father, and he shall be to me a son: and my mercy will I not withdraw from him, as I withdrew \add it\add* from them who were before you.  
\v 14 And I will establish him in my house and in his kingdom for ever; and his throne shall be set up for ever.   
\p
\v 15 According to all these words, and according to all this vision, so spoke Nathan to David.   
\p
\v 16 And king David came and sat before the Lord, and said, Who am I, O Lord God? and what \add is\add* my house, that you have loved me for ever?  
\v 17 And these things were little in your sight, O God: you have also spoken concerning the house of your servant for a long time to come, and you have looked upon me as a man looks upon his fellow, and have exalted me, O Lord God.  
\v 18 What shall David do more toward you to glorify \add you\add*? and you know your servant.  
\v 19 And you have worked all this greatness according to yours heart.  
\v 20 O Lord, there is none like you, and there is no God beside you, according to all things which we have heard with our ears.  
\v 21 Nor is there another nation upon the earth \add such\add* as your people Israel, whereas God led him in the way, to redeem a people for himself, to make for himself a great and glorious name, to cast out nations from before your people, whom you redeemedst out of Egypt.  
\v 22 And you have appointed your people Israel as a people to yourself for ever; and you, Lord, did become a God to them.  
\v 23 And now, Lord, let the word which you spoke to your servant, and concerning his house, be confirmed for ever, and do you as you have spoken.  
\v 24 And let your name \add be\add* established and magnified for ever, \add men\add* saying, Lord, Lord, Almighty God of Israel: and \add let\add* the house of your servant David \add be\add* established before you.  
\v 25 For you, O Lord my God, have revealed to the ear of your servant that you will build him a house; therefore your servant has found a willingness to pray before you.  
\v 26 And now, Lord, you yourself art God, and you have spoken these good things concerning your servant.  
\v 27 And now you have begun to bless the house of your servant, so that it should continue for ever before you: for you, Lord, have blessed \add it\add*, and do you bless \add it\add* for ever.   
\c 18  
\p
\v 1 And it came to pass afterwards, that David struck the Philistines, and routed them, and took Geth and its villages out of the hand of the Philistines.   
\p
\v 2 And he struck Moab; and the Moabites became servants to David, \add and\add* tributaries.   
\p
\v 3 And David struck Adraazar king of Suba of Hamath, as he was going to establish power toward the river Euphrates.  
\v 4 And David took of them a thousand chariots, and seven thousand horsemen, and twenty thousand infantry: and David houghed all the chariot \add horses\add*, but there were reserved of them a hundred chariots.  
\v 5 And the Syrian came from Damascus to help Adraazar king of Suba; and David struck of the Syrian \add army\add* twenty and two thousand men.  
\v 6 And David put a garrison in Syria near Damascus; and they became tributary servants to David: and the Lord delivered David wherever he went.  
\v 7 And David took the golden collars that were on the servants of Adraazar, and brought them to Jerusalem.  
\v 8 And David took out of Matabs, and out of the chief cities of Adraazar very much brass: of this Solomon made the brazen sea, and the pillars, and the brazen vessels.   
\p
\v 9 And Thoa king of Hamath heard that David had smitten the whole force of Adraazar king of Suba.  
\v 10 And he sent Aduram his son to king David to ask how he was, and to congratulate him because he had fought against Adraazar, and smitten him; for Thoa was the enemy of Adraazar.  
\v 11 And all the golden and silver and brazen vessels, even these king David consecrated to the Lord, with the silver and the gold which he took from all the nations; from Idumæa, and Moab, and from the children of Ammon, and from the Philistines, and from Amalek.   
\p
\v 12 And Abesa son of Zeruiah struck the Idumeans in the valley of Salt, eighteen thousand.  
\v 13 And he put garrisons in the valley; and all the Idumæans became David's servants: and the Lord delivered David wherever he went.   
\p
\v 14 So David reigned over all Israel; and he executed judgment and justice to all his people.  
\v 15 And Joab the son of Zeruiah \add was\add* over the army, and Josaphat the son of Achilud \add was\add* recorder.  
\v 16 And Zadok son of Ahitub, and Ahimelech son of Abiathar, \add were\add* the priests; and Susa \add was\add* the scribe;  
\v 17 and Benaiah the son of Jodae \add was\add* over the Cherethite and the Phelethite, and the sons of David were the chief deputies of the king.   
\c 19  
\p
\v 1 And it came to pass after this, \add that\add* Ir-nahash the king of the children of Ammon died, and Anan his son reigned in his stead.  
\v 2 And David said, I will act kindly toward Anan the son of Ir-nahash, as his father acted kindly towards me. And David sent messengers to condole with him on the death of his father. So the servants of David came into the land of the children of Ammon to Anan, to comfort him.  
\v 3 And the chiefs of the children of Ammon said to Anan, Is it to honour your father before you, that David has sent comforters to you? Have not his servants come to you that they might search the city, and to spy out the land?  
\v 4 And Anan took the servants of David, and shaved them, and cut off the half of their garments as far as their tunic, and sent them away.  
\v 5 And there came men to report to David concerning the men: and he sent to meet them, for they were greatly disgraced: and the king said, Dwell in Jericho until your beards have grown, and return.   
\p
\v 6 And the children of Ammon saw that the people of David were ashamed, and Anan and the children of Ammon sent a thousand talents of silver to hire for themselves chariots and horsemen out of Syria of Mesopotamia, and out of Syria Maacha, and from Shobal.  
\v 7 And they hired for themselves two and thirty thousand chariots, and the king of Maacha and his people; and they came and camped before Medaba: and the children of Ammon assembled out of their cities, and came to fight.   
\p
\v 8 And David heard, and sent Joab and all the host of mighty men.  
\v 9 And the children of Ammon came forth, and set themselves in array for battle by the gate of the city: and the kings that were come forth camped by themselves in the plain.  
\v 10 And Joab saw that they were fronting \add him\add* to fight against him before and behind, and he chose \add Shammah\add* out of all the young men of Israel, and they set themselves in array against the Syrian.  
\v 11 And the rest of the people he gave into the hand of his brother Abesai, and they set themselves in array against the children of Ammon.  
\v 12 And he said, If the Syrian should prevail against me, then shall you deliver me: and if the children of Ammon should prevail against you, then will I deliver you.  
\v 13 Be of good courage, and let us be strong, for our people, and for the cities of our God: and the Lord shall do what \add is\add* good in his eyes.   
\p
\v 14 So Joab and the people who were with him set themselves in battle array against the Syrians, and they fled from them.  
\v 15 And the children of Ammon saw that the Syrians fled, and they also fled from before Abesai, and from before Joab his brother, and they came to the city: and Joab came to Jerusalem.   
\p
\v 16 And the Syrian saw that Israel had defeated him, and he sent messengers, and they brought out the Syrians from beyond the river; and Sophath the commander-in-chief of the forces of Adraazar \add was\add* before them.  
\v 17 And it was told David; and he gathered all Israel, and crossed over Jordan, and came upon them, and set the battle in array against them. So David set \add his army\add* in array to fight against the Syrians, and they fought against him.  
\v 18 And the Syrians fled from before Israel; and David slew of the Syrians seven thousand \add riders in\add* chariots, and forty thousand infantry, and he slew Sophath the commander-in-chief of the forces.  
\v 19 And the servants of Adraazar saw that they were defeated before Israel, and they made peace with David and served him: and the Syrians would not any more help the children of Ammon.   
\c 20  
\p
\v 1 And it came to pass at the return of the year, at the \add time of the\add* going forth of kings \add to war\add*, that Joab gathered the whole force of the army, and they ravaged the land of the children of Ammon; and he came and besieged Rabba. But David abode in Jerusalem. And Joab struck Rabba and destroyed it.  
\v 2 And David took the crown of Molchom their king off his head, and the weight of it was found \add to be\add* a talent of gold, and on it were precious stones; and it was \add placed\add* on the head of David: and he brought out the spoils of the city \add which were\add* very great.  
\v 3 And he brought out the people who were in it, and sawed them apart with saws, and \add cut them\add* with iron axes, and with harrows: and thus David did to all the children of Ammon. And David and all his people returned to Jerusalem.   
\p
\v 4 And it came to pass afterward that there was again war with the Philistines in Gezer: then Sibbecai the Sosathite struck Saphut of the sons of the giants, and laid him low.   
\p
\v 5 And there \add was\add* war again with the Philistines; and Elhanan the son of Jair struck Lachmi the brother of Goliath the Gittite, and the wood of his spear \add was\add* as a weavers' beam.   
\p
\v 6 And there was again war in Geth, and there was a man of extraordinary size, and his fingers \add and toes were\add* six on each hand and foot, four and twenty; and he was descended from the giants.  
\v 7 And he defied Israel, and Jonathan the son of Samaa the brother of David slew him.  
\v 8 These were born to Rapha in Geth; all four were giants, and they fell by the hand of David, and by the hand of his servants.   
\c 21  
\p
\v 1 And the devil stood up against Israel, and moved David to number Israel.  
\v 2 And king David said to Joab and to the captains of the forces, Go, number Israel from Bathsheba even to Dan, and bring me \add the account\add*, and I shall know their number.  
\v 3 And Joab said, May the Lord add to his people, a hundred-fold as many as they \add are\add*, and \add let\add* the eyes of my lord the king see \add it\add*: all \add are\add* the servants of my lord. Why does my lord seek this thing? \add do it not\add*, lest it become a sin to Israel.  
\v 4 Nevertheless the king's word prevailed against Joab; and Joab went out and passed through all Israel, and came to Jerusalem.  
\v 5 And Joab gave the number of the mustering of the people to David: and all Israel was a million and a hundred thousand men who drew sword: and the sons of Judah \add were\add* four hundred and seventy thousand men who drew sword.  
\v 6 But he numbered not Levi and Benjamin among them; for the word of the king was painful to Joab.   
\p
\v 7 And \add there was\add* evil in the sight of the Lord respecting this thing; and he struck Israel.  
\v 8 And David said to God, I have sinned exceedingly, in that I have done this thing: and now, I pray you, remove the sin of your servant; for I have been exceedingly foolish.   
\p
\v 9 And the Lord spoke to Gad the seer, saying,  
\v 10 Go and speak to David, saying, Thus saith the Lord, I bring three things upon you: choose one of them for yourself, and I will do it to you.  
\v 11 And Gad came to David, and said to him, Thus saith the Lord, Choose for yourself,  
\v 12 either three years of famine, or that you should flee three months from the face of yours enemies, and the sword of yours enemies \add shall be employed\add* to destroy you, or that the sword of the Lord and pestilence \add should be\add* three days in the land, and the angel of the Lord \add shall be\add* destroying in all the inheritance of Israel. And now consider what I shall answer to him that sent the message.   
\p
\v 13 And David said to Gad, They are very hard for me, even \add all\add* the three: let me fall now into the hands of the Lord, for his mercies \add are\add* very abundant, and let me not fall by any means into the hands of man.   
\p
\v 14 So the Lord brought pestilence upon Israel: and there fell of Israel seventy thousand men.  
\v 15 And God sent an angel to Jerusalem to destroy it: and as he was destroying, the Lord saw, and repented for the evil, and said to the angel that was destroying, Let it suffice you; withhold yours hand. And the angel of the Lord stood by the threshing-floor of Arnan the Jebusite.  
\v 16 And David lifted up his eyes, and saw the angel of the Lord, standing between the earth and the heaven, and his sword drawn in his hand, stretched out over Jerusalem: and David and the elders clothed in sackcloth, fell upon their faces.  
\v 17 And David said to God, \add Was it\add* not I \add that\add* gave orders to number the people? and I am the guilty one; I have greatly sinned: but these sheep, what have they done? O Lord God, let your hand be upon me, and upon my father's house, and not on your people for destruction, O Lord!   
\p
\v 18 And the angel of the Lord told Gad to tell David, that he should go up to erect an altar to the Lord, in the threshing-floor of Arnan the Jebusite.  
\v 19 And David went up according to the word of Gad, which he spoke in the name of the Lord.  
\v 20 And Arnan turned and saw the king; and he hid himself and his four sons with him. Now Arnan was threshing wheat.  
\v 21 And David came to Arnan; and Arnan came forth from the threshing-floor, and did homage to David with his face to the ground.  
\v 22 And David said to Arnan, Give me your place of the threshing-floor, and I will build upon it an altar to the Lord: give it me for its worth in money, and the plague shall cease from \add among\add* the people.  
\v 23 And Arnan said to David, Take it to yourself, and let my lord the king do what is right in his eyes: see, I have given the calves for a whole-burnt-offering, and the plough for wood, and the corn for a meat-offering; I have given all.  
\v 24 And king David said to Arnan, No; for I will surely buy it for its worth in money: for I will not take your property for the Lord, to offer a whole-burnt-offering to the Lord without cost \add to myself\add*.  
\v 25 And David gave to Arnan for his place six hundred shekels of gold \add by\add* weight.  
\v 26 And David built there an altar to the Lord, and offered up whole-burnt-offerings and peace-offerings: and he cried to the Lord, and he answered him by fire out of heaven on the altar of whole-burnt-offerings, and \add it\add* consumed the whole-burnt-offering.  
\v 27 And the Lord spoke to the angel; and he put up the sword into its sheath.   
\p
\v 28 At that time when David saw that the Lord answered him in the threshing-floor of Arnan the Jebusite, he also sacrificed there.  
\v 29 And the tabernacle of the Lord which Moses made in the wilderness, and the altar of whole-burnt-offerings, \add were\add* at that time in the high place at Gibeon.  
\v 30 And David could not go before it to inquire of God; for he hasted not because of the sword of the angel of the Lord.   
\c 22  
\p
\v 1 And David said, This is the house of the Lord God, and this \add is\add* the altar for whole-burnt-offering for Israel.   
\p
\v 2 And David gave orders to gather all the strangers that were in the land of Israel; and he appointed stone-hewers to hew polished stones to build the house to God.  
\v 3 And David prepared much iron for the nails of the doors and the gates; the hinges also and brass in abundance, there was no weighing \add of it\add*.  
\v 4 And cedar trees without number: for the Sidonians and the Tyrians brought cedar trees in abundance to David.  
\v 5 And David said, My son Solomon \add is\add* a tender child, and the house \add for me\add* to build to the Lord \add is\add* for superior magnificence for a name and for a glory through all the earth: I will make preparation for it. And David prepared abundantly before his death.   
\p
\v 6 And he called Solomon his son, and commanded him to build the house for the Lord God of Israel.  
\v 7 And David said to Solomon, \add My\add* child, it was in my heart to build a house to the name of the Lord God.  
\v 8 But the word of the Lord came to me, saying, You have shed blood abundantly, and have carried on great wars: you shall not build a house to my name, because you have shed much blood upon the earth before me.  
\v 9 Behold, a son shall be born to you, he shall be a man of rest; and I will give him rest from all his enemies round about: for his name \add shall be\add* Solomon, and I will give peace and quietness to Israel in his days.  
\v 10 He shall build a house to my name; and he shall be a son to me, and I will be a father to him; and I will establish the throne of his kingdom in Israel for ever.  
\v 11 And now, my son, the Lord shall be with you, and prosper \add you\add*; and you shall build a house to the Lord your God, as he spoke concerning you.  
\v 12 Only may the Lord give you wisdom and prudence, and strengthen you over Israel, both to keep and to do the law of the Lord your God.  
\v 13 Then will he prosper \add you\add*, if you take care to do the commandments and judgments which the Lord commanded Moses for Israel: be courageous and strong; fear not, nor be terrified.   
\p
\v 14 And, behold, I according to my poverty have prepared for the house of the Lord a hundred thousand talents of gold, and a million talents of silver, and brass and iron without measure; for it is abundant; and I have prepared timber and stones; and do you add to these.  
\v 15 And \add of them who are\add* with you do you add to the multitude of workmen; \add let there be\add* artificers and masons, and carpenters, and every skilful \add workman\add* in every work;  
\v 16 in gold and silver, brass and iron, \add of which\add* there is no number. Arise and do, and the Lord \add be\add* with you.   
\p
\v 17 And David charged all the chief men of Israel to help Solomon his son, \add saying\add*,  
\v 18 \add Is\add* not the Lord with you? and he has given you rest round about, for he has given into your hands the inhabitants of the land; and the land is subdued before the Lord, and before his people.  
\v 19 Now set your hearts and souls to seek after the Lord your God: and rise, and build a sanctuary to your God to carry in the ark of the covenant of the Lord, and the holy vessels of God, into the house that is to be built to the name of the Lord.   
\c 23  
\p
\v 1 And David was old and full of days; and he made Solomon his son king over Israel in his stead.  
\v 2 And he assembled all the chief men of Israel, and the priests, and the Levites.  
\v 3 And the Levites numbered \add themselves\add* from thirty years old and upward; and their number by their polls amounted to thirty and eight thousand men.  
\v 4 Of the overseers over the works of the house of the Lord \add there were\add* twenty-four thousand, and \add there were\add* six thousand scribes and judges;  
\v 5 and four thousand door-keepers, and four thousand to praise the Lord with instruments which he made to praise the Lord.   
\p
\v 6 And David divided them \add into\add* daily courses, for the sons of Levi, for Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.  
\v 7 And for \add the family of\add* Gershon, Edan, and Semei.  
\v 8 The sons of Edan \add were\add* Jeiel, the chief, and Zethan, and Joel, three.  
\v 9 The sons of Semei; Salomith, Jeiel, and Dan, three: these \add were\add* the chiefs of the families of Edan.  
\v 10 And to the sons of Semei, Jahath, and Ziza, and Joash, and Beria: these \add were\add* the four sons of Semei.  
\v 11 And Jahath was the chief, and Ziza the second: and Joash and Beria did not multiply sons, and they became \add only\add* one reckoning according to the house of their father.   
\p
\v 12 The sons of Kohath; Amram, Isaar, Hebron, Oziel, four.  
\v 13 The sons of Amram; Aaron and Moses: and Aaron was appointed for the consecration of the most holy things, he and his sons for ever, to burn incense before the Lord, to minister and bless in his name for ever.  
\v 14 And \add as for\add* Moses the man of God, his sons were reckoned to the tribe of Levi.  
\v 15 The sons of Moses; Gershom, and Eliezer.  
\v 16 The sons of Gershom; Shebuel the chief.  
\v 17 And the sons of Eliezer were, Rabia the chief: and Eliezer had no other sons; but the sons of Rabia were very greatly multiplied.  
\v 18 The sons of Isaar; Salomoth the chief.  
\v 19 The sons of Hebron; Jeria the chief, Amaria the second, Jahaziel the third, Jekemias the fourth.  
\v 20 The sons of Oziel; Micha the chief, and Isshiah the second.   
\p
\v 21 The sons of Merari; Mahli, and Mushi: the sons of Mahli; Eleazar, and Kish.  
\v 22 And Eleazar died, and he had no sons, but daughters: and the sons of Kish, their brothers, took them.  
\v 23 The sons of Mushi; Mahli, and Eder, and Jarimoth, three.   
\p
\v 24 These \add are\add* the sons of Levi according to the houses of their fathers; chiefs of their families according to their numbering, according to the number of their names, according to their polls, doing the works of service of the house of the Lord, from twenty years old and upward.  
\v 25 For David said, The Lord God of Israel has given rest to his people, and has taken up his abode in Jerusalem for ever.  
\v 26 And the Levites bore not the tabernacle, and all the vessels of it for its service.  
\v 27 For by the last words of David was the number of the Levites \add taken\add* from twenty years old and upward.  
\v 28 For he appointed them to wait on Aaron, to minister in the house of the Lord, over the courts, and over the chambers, and over the purification of all the holy things, and over the works of the service of the house of God;  
\v 29 and for the show-bread, and for the fine flour of the meat-offering, and for the unleavened cakes, and for the fried cake, and for the dough, and for every measure;  
\v 30 and to stand in the morning to praise and give thanks to the Lord, and so in the evening;  
\v 31 and \add to be\add* over all the whole-burnt-offerings that were offered up to the Lord on the sabbaths, and at the new moons, and at the feasts, by number, according to the order \add given\add* to them, continually before the Lord.  
\v 32 And they are to keep the charge of the tabernacle of witness, and the charge of the holy place, and the charges of the sons of Aaron their brothers, to minister in the house of the Lord.   
\c 24  
\p
\v 1 And \add they number\add* the sons of Aaron in \add their\add* division, Nadab, and Abiud, and Eleazar, and Ithamar.  
\v 2 And Nadab and Abiud died before their father, and they had no sons: so Eleazar and Ithamar the sons of Aaron ministered as priests.  
\v 3 And David distributed them, even Zadok of the sons of Eleazar, and Ahimelech of the sons of Ithamar, according to their numbering, according to their service, according to the houses of their fathers.   
\p
\v 4 And there were found \add among\add* the sons of Eleazar more chiefs of the mighty ones, than of the sons of Ithamar: and he divided them, sixteen heads of families to the sons of Eleazar, eight according to \add their\add* families to the sons of Ithamar.  
\v 5 And he divided them according to their lots, one with the other; for there were those who had charge of the holy things, and those who had charge of the \add house\add* of the Lord among the sons of Eleazar, and among the sons of Ithamar.   
\p
\v 6 And Samaias the son of Nethanel, the scribe, \add of the family\add* of Levi, wrote them down before the king, and the princes, and Zadok the priest, and Ahimelech the son of Abiathar \add were present\add*; and the heads of the families of the priests and the Levites, each of a household \add were assigned\add* one to Eleazar, and one to Ithamar.   
\p
\v 7 And the first lot came out to Jehoiarib, the second to Jedia,  
\v 8 the third to Harim, the fourth to Seorim,  
\v 9 the fifth to Melchias, the sixth to Mijamin,  
\v 10 the seventh to Hakkoz, the eighth to Abijah,  
\v 11 the ninth to Jesus, the tenth to Shecaniah,  
\v 12 the eleventh to Eliashib, the twelfth to Jakim,  
\v 13 the thirteenth to Huppah, the fourteenth to Jeshebeab,  
\v 14 the fifteenth to Bilgah, the sixteenth to Immer,  
\v 15 the seventeenth to Hezir, the eighteenth to Happizzez,  
\v 16 the nineteenth to Pethahiah, the twentis to Jehezkel,  
\v 17 the twenty-first to Ahiam, the twenty-second to Gamul,  
\v 18 the twenty-third to Delaiah, the twenty-fourth to Maaziah.   
\p
\v 19 This \add is\add* their numbering according to their service to go into the house of the Lord, according to their appointment by the hand of Aaron their father, as the Lord God of Israel commanded.   
\p
\v 20 And for the sons of Levi that were left, \add even\add* for the sons of Amram, Shubael: for the sons of Shubael, Jedia.  
\v 21 For Rehabiah, the chief \add was Isaari\add*,  
\v 22 and for Isaari, Salomoth: for the sons of Salomoth, Jahath.  
\v 23 The sons of Hebron; Jeriah the second, Jahaziel the third, Jekameam the fourth.  
\v 24 For the sons of Oziel, Micha: the sons of Micha; Shamir.  
\v 25 The brother of Micha; Isshiah, the son of Isshiah; Zechariah.  
\v 26 The sons of Merari, Mahli, and Mushi: the sons of Ozia,  
\v 27 \add That is, the sons\add* of Merari by Ozia,—his sons \add were\add* Beno, and Zaccur, and Abai.  
\v 28 To Mahli \add were born\add* Eleazar, and Ithamar; and Eleazar died, and had no sons.  
\v 29 For Kish; the sons of Kish; Jerameel.  
\v 30 And the sons of Mushi; Mahli, and Eder, and Jerimoth. These \add were\add* the sons of the Levites according to the houses of their families.  
\v 31 And they also received lots as their brothers the sons of Aaron before the king; Zadok also, and Ahimelech, and the chiefs of the families of the priests and of the Levites, principal heads of families, even as their younger brothers.   
\c 25  
\p
\v 1 And king David and the captains of the host appointed to their services the sons of Asaph, and of Heman, and of Jeduthun, prophesiers with harps, and lutes, and cymbals: and their number was according to their polls serving in their ministrations.   
\p
\v 2 The sons of Asaph; Zaccur, Joseph, and Nethaniah, and Asarelah: the sons of Asaph \add were\add* next the king.   
\p
\v 3 To Jeduthun \add were reckoned\add* the sons of Jeduthun, Gedaliah, and Zeri, and Jeshaiah, and Hashabiah, and Mattithiah, six after their father Jeduthun, sounding loudly on the harp thanksgiving and praise to the Lord.   
\p
\v 4 To Heman \add were reckoned\add* the sons of Heman, Bukkiah, and Mattaniah, and Oziel, and Shebuel, and Jerimoth, and Ananias, and Anan, and Eliathah, and Giddalti, and Romamti-ezer, and Joshbekashah, and Mallothi, and Hothir, and Mahazioth.  
\v 5 All these \add were\add* the sons of Heman the king's chief player in the praises of God, to lift up the horn. And God gave to Heman fourteen sons, and three daughters.  
\v 6 All these sang hymns with their father in the house of God, with cymbals, and lutes, and harps, for the service of the house of God, near the king, and Asaph, and Jeduthun, and Heman.   
\p
\v 7 And the number of them after their brothers, those instructed to sing to God, every one that understood \add singing\add* was two hundred and eighty-eight.   
\p
\v 8 And they also cast lots for the daily courses, for the great and the small \add of them\add*, of the perfect ones and the learners.  
\v 9 And the first lot of his sons and of his brothers came forth to Asaph the son of Joseph, \add namely\add*, Gedaliah: the second Gedaliah, his sons and his brothers \add being\add* twelve.  
\v 10 The third Zacchur, his sons and his brothers \add were\add* twelve:  
\v 11 the fourth Izri, his sons and his brothers \add were\add* twelve:  
\v 12 the fifth Nathan, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 13 the sixth Bukkiah, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 14 the seventh Jesarelah, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 15 the eighth Josia, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 16 the ninth Mattaniah, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 17 the tenth Semeia, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 18 the eleventh Asriel, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 19 the twelfth Asabia, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 20 the thirteenth Shebuel, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 21 the fourteenth Mattithiah, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 22 the fifteenth Jerimoth, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 23 the sixteenth Hananiah, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 24 the seventeenth Joshbekashah, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 25 the eighteenth Ananias, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 26 the nineteenth Mallothi, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 27 the twentis Eliathah, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 28 the twenty-first Hothir, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 29 the twenty-second Giddalti, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 30 the twenty-third Mahazioth, his sons and his brothers, twelve:  
\v 31 the twenty-fourth Romamti-ezer, his sons and his brothers, twelve.   
\c 26  
\p
\v 1 And for the divisions of the gates: the sons of the Corites \add were\add* Meshelemiah, of the sons of Asaph.  
\v 2 And Meshelemiah's first-born son \add was\add* Zacharias, the second Jediael, the third Zebadiah, the fourth Jathniel,  
\v 3 the fifth Elam, the sixth Jonathan, the seventh Eliehoenai, the eighth Obed-edom.  
\v 4 And to Obed-edom \add there were born\add* sons, Samaias the first-born, Jozabath the second, Joah the third, Sachar the fourth, Nethanel the fifth,  
\v 5 Ammiel the sixth, Issachar the seventh, Peullethai the eighth: for God blessed him.  
\v 6 And to Samaias his son were born the sons of his first-born, chiefs over the house of their father, for they were mighty.  
\v 7 The sons of Samai; Othni, and Rephael, and Obed, and Elzabad, and Achiud, mighty men, Elihu, and Semachiah, and Isbacom.  
\v 8 All \add these were\add* of the sons of Obed-edom, they and their sons and their brothers, doing mightily in service: in all sixty-two \add born\add* to Obed-edom.   
\p
\v 9 And Meshelemiah \add had\add* eighteen sons and brothers, mighty men.  
\v 10 And to Hosah of the sons of Merari \add there were born\add* sons, keeping the dominion; though he was not the first-born, yet his father made him chief of the second division.  
\v 11 Hilkiah the second, Tebaliah the third, Zacharias the fourth: all these \add were\add* the sons and brothers of Hosah, thirteen.   
\p
\v 12 To these \add were assigned\add* the divisions of the gates, to the chiefs of the mighty men the daily courses, even their brothers, to minister in the house of the Lord.  
\v 13 And they cast lots for the small as well as for the great, for the several gates, according to their families.  
\v 14 And the lot of the east gates fell to Shelemiah, and Zacharias: the sons of Soaz cast lots for Melchias, and the lot came out northward.  
\v 15 To Obed-edom \add they gave by lot\add* the south, opposite the house of Esephim.  
\v 16 \add They gave the lot\add* for the second to Hosah westward, after the gate of the chamber by the ascent, watch against watch.  
\v 17 Eastward \add were\add* six \add watchmen\add* in the day; northward four by the day; southward four by the day; and two at the Esephim,  
\v 18 to relieve guard, also for Hosah westward after the chamber-gate, three. \add There was\add* a ward over against the ward of the ascent eastward, six \add men\add* in a day, and four for the north, and four for the south, and at the Esephim two to relieve guard, and four by the west, and two to relieve guard at the pathway.  
\v 19 These \add are\add* the divisions of the porters for the sons of Korah, and to the sons of Merari.   
\p
\v 20 And the Levites their brothers \add were\add* over the treasures of the house of the Lord, and over the treasures of the hallowed things.  
\v 21 These \add were\add* the sons of Ladan, the sons of the Gershonite: to Ladan \add belonged\add* the heads of the families: \add the son\add* of Ladan the Gershonite \add was\add* Jeiel.  
\v 22 The sons of Jeiel \add were\add* Zetham, and Joel; brothers \add who were\add* over the treasures of the house of the Lord.  
\v 23 To Amram and Issaar belonged Hebron, and Oziel.  
\v 24 And Shebuel the \add son\add* of Gershom, the \add son\add* of Moses, \add was\add* over the treasures.  
\v 25 And Rabias \add was\add* son to his brother Eliezer, and \add so was\add* Josias, and Joram, and Zichri, and Salomoth.  
\v 26 This Salomoth and his brothers \add were\add* over all the sacred treasures, which David the king and the heads of families consecrated, \add and\add* the captains of thousands and captains of hundreds, and princes of the host,  
\v 27 things which he took out of cities and from the spoils, and consecrated Shammah of them, so that the building of the house of God should not want \add supplies\add*;  
\v 28 and over all the holy things of God dedicated by Samuel the prophet, and Saul the son of Kish, and Abner the son of Ner, and Joab the son of Zeruiah, whatever they sanctified \add was\add* by the hand of Salomoth and his brothers.   
\p
\v 29 For the Issaarites, Chenaniah, and \add his\add* sons \add were over\add* the outward ministration over Israel, to record and to judge.  
\v 30 For the Hebronites, Hashabiah and his brothers, a thousand and seven hundred mighty men, \add were\add* over the charge of Israel beyond Jordan westward, for all the service of the Lord and work of the king.  
\v 31 Of the \add family\add* of Hebron Uriah \add was\add* chief, even of the Hebronites according to their generations, according to their families. In the fortis year of his reign they were numbered, and there were found mighty men among them in Jazer of Gilead.  
\v 32 And his brothers \add were\add* two thousand seven hundred mighty men, chiefs of their families, and king David set them over the Reubenites, and the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh, for every ordinance of the Lord, and business of the king.   
\c 27  
\p
\v 1 Now the sons of Israel according to their number, heads of families, captains of thousands and captains of hundreds, and scribes ministering to the king, and for every affair of the king according to \add their\add* divisions, \add for\add* every ordinance of coming in and going out monthly, for all the months of the year, one division of them \add was\add* twenty-four thousand.   
\p
\v 2 And over the first division of the first month \add was\add* Jashobeam the son of Zabdiel: in his division \add were\add* twenty-four thousand.  
\v 3 Of the sons of Perez \add one\add* was chief of all the captains of the host for the first month.  
\v 4 And over the division of the second month \add was\add* Dodai the son of Ahohite, and over his division \add was\add* Mikloth also chief: and in his division \add were\add* twenty and four thousand, chief men of the host.  
\v 5 The third for the third month \add was\add* Benaiah the son of Jodae the chief priest: and in his division \add were\add* twenty and four thousand.  
\v 6 This Benaiah \add was\add* more mighty than the thirty, and over the thirty: and Zabad his son \add was\add* over his division.  
\v 7 The fourth for the fourth month \add was\add* Asahel the brother of Joab, and Zebadiah his son, and his brothers: and in his division \add were\add* twenty and four thousand.  
\v 8 The fifth chief for the fifth month \add was\add* Shammoth the Izrahite: and in his division \add were\add* twenty and four thousand.  
\v 9 The sixth for the sixth month \add was\add* Hoduias the son of Ekkes the Tekoite: and in his division \add were\add* twenty and four thousand.  
\v 10 The seventh for the seventh month \add was\add* Helez of Phallus of the children of Ephraim: and in his division \add were\add* twenty and four thousand.  
\v 11 The eighth for the eighth month \add was\add* Sibbecai the Hushathite, \add belonging\add* to Zerahite: and in his division \add were\add* twenty and four thousand.  
\v 12 The ninth for the ninth month \add was\add* Abiezer of Anathoth, of the land of Benjamin: and in his division \add were\add* twenty and four thousand.  
\v 13 The tenth for the tenth month \add was\add* Maharai the Netophathite, \add belonging\add* to Zerahite: and in his division \add were\add* twenty and four thousand.  
\v 14 The eleventh for the eleventh month \add was\add* Benaiah of Pirathonite, of the sons of Ephraim: and in his division \add were\add* twenty and four thousand.  
\v 15 The twelfth for the twelfth month \add was\add* Heldai the Netophathite, \add belonging\add* to Othniel: and in his division \add were\add* twenty and four thousand.   
\p
\v 16 And over the tribes of Israel, the chief for Reuben \add was\add* Eliezer the son of Zichri: for Simeon, Saphatias the son of Maacha:  
\v 17 for Levi, Hashabiah the son of Kemuel: for Aaron, Zadok:  
\v 18 for Judah, Eliab of the brothers of David: for Issachar, Omri the son of Michael:  
\v 19 for Zebulun, Samæas the son of Obadiah: for Naphtali, Jerimoth the son of Oziel:  
\v 20 for Ephraim, Hoshea the son of Ozia: for the half-tribe of Manasseh, Joel the son of Pedaiah:  
\v 21 for the half-tribe of Manasseh in the land of Gilead, Iddo the son of Zechariah, for the sons of Benjamin, Jaasiel the son of Abner:  
\v 22 for Dan, Azarel the son of Jeroham: these \add are\add* the chiefs of the tribes of Israel.   
\p
\v 23 But David took not their number from twenty years old and under: because the Lord said that he would multiply Israel as the stars of the heaven.  
\v 24 And Joab the son of Zeruiah began to number the people, and did not finish the work, for there was hereupon wrath on Israel; and the number was not recorded in the book of the chronicles of king David.   
\p
\v 25 And over the king's treasures \add was\add* Asmoth the son of Adiel; and over the treasures in the country, and in the towns, and in the villages, and in the towers, \add was\add* Jonathan the son of Ozia.  
\v 26 And over the husbandmen who tilled the ground \add was\add* Ezri the son of Chelub.  
\v 27 And over the fields \add was\add* Semei of Ramathite; and over the treasures of wine in the fields \add was\add* Zabdi the son of Shiphmite.  
\v 28 And over the oliveyards, and over the sycamores in the plain country \add was\add* Ballanan the Gederite; and over the stores of oil \add was\add* Joash.  
\v 29 And over the oxen pasturing in Sharon \add was\add* Shitrai the Sharonite; and over the oxen in the valleys \add was\add* Sophat the son of Adlai.  
\v 30 And over the camels \add was\add* Abijah the Ishmaelite; and over the asses \add was\add* Jehdeiah of Meronothite.  
\v 31 And over the sheep \add was\add* Jaziz the Hagrite. All these \add were\add* superintendents of the substance of king David.   
\p
\v 32 And Jonathan, David's uncle by the father's side, \add was\add* a counsellor, a wise man: and Jehiel the son of Hachmoni \add was\add* with the king's sons.  
\v 33 Ahithophel \add was\add* the king's counsellor: and Hushai the chief friend of the king.  
\v 34 And after this Ahithophel Jodae the son of Benaiah \add came\add* next, and Abiathar: and Joab \add was\add* the king's commander-in-chief.   
\c 28  
\p
\v 1 And David assembled all the chief \add men\add* of Israel, the chief of the judges, and all the chief \add men\add* of the courses \add of attendance\add* on the person of the king, and the captains of thousands and hundreds, and the treasurers, and the lords of his substance, and of all the king's property, and of his sons, together with the eunuchs, and the mighty men, and the warriors of the army, at Jerusalem.   
\p
\v 2 And David stood in the midst of the assembly, and said, Hear me, my brothers, and my people: it was in my heart to build a house of rest for the ark of the covenant of the Lord, and a place for the feet of our Lord, and I prepared \add materials\add* suitable for the building:  
\v 3 but God said, You shall not build me a house to call my name upon it, for you are a man of war, and have shed blood.  
\v 4 Yet the Lord God of Israel chose me out of the whole house of my father to be king over Israel for ever; and he chose Judah as the kingly \add house\add*, and out of the house of Judah \add he chose\add* the house of my father; and among the sons of my father he preferred me, that I should be king over all Israel.  
\v 5 And of all my sons, (for the Lord has given me many sons,) he has chosen Solomon my son, to set him on the throne of the kingdom of the Lord over Israel.  
\v 6 And God said to me, Solomon your son shall build my house and my court: for I have chosen him to be my son, and I will be to him a father.  
\v 7 And I will establish his kingdom for ever, if he continue to keep my commandments, and my judgments, as \add at\add* this day.  
\v 8 And now \add I charge you\add* before the whole assembly of the Lord, and in the audience of our God, keep and seek all the commandments of the Lord our God, that you may inherit the good land, and leave it for your sons to inherit after you for ever.   
\p
\v 9 And now, \add my\add* son Solomon, know the God of your fathers, and serve him with a perfect heart and willing soul: for the Lord searches all hearts, and knows every thought: if you seek him, he will be found of you; but if you should forsake him, he will forsake you for ever.  
\v 10 See now, for the Lord has chosen you to build him a house for a sanctuary, be strong and do \add it\add*.   
\p
\v 11 And David gave Solomon his son the plan of the temple, and its buildings, and its treasuries, and its upper chambers, and the inner store-rooms, and the place of the atonement,  
\v 12 and the plan which he had in his mind of the courts of the house of the Lord, and of all the chambers round about, \add designed\add* for the treasuries of the house of God, and of the treasuries of the holy things, and of the chambers for resting:  
\v 13 and \add the plan\add* of the courses of the priests and Levites, for all the work of the service of the house of the Lord, and of the stores of vessels for ministration of the service of the house of the Lord.  
\v 14 And \add he gave him\add* the account of their weight, both of gold and silver \add vessels\add*.  
\v 15 He gave him the weight of the candlesticks, and of the lamps.  
\v 16 He gave him likewise the weight of the tables of shewbread, of each table of gold, and likewise of the \add tables of\add* silver:  
\v 17 also of the flesh-hooks, and vessels for drink-offering, and golden bowls: and the weight of the gold and silver \add articles\add*, and censers, \add and\add* bowls, according to the weight of each.  
\v 18 And he showed him the weight \add of the utensils\add* of the altar of incense, \add which was\add* of pure gold, and the plan of the chariot of the cherubs that spread out their wings, and overshadowed the ark of the covenant of the Lord.  
\v 19 David gave all to Solomon in the Lord's handwriting, according to the knowledge given him of the work of the pattern.   
\p
\v 20 And David said to Solomon his son, Be strong, and play the man, and do: fear not, neither be terrified; for the Lord my God \add is\add* with you; he will not forsake you, and will not fail you, until you have finished all the work of the service of the house of the Lord. And behold the pattern of the temple, even his house, and its treasury, and the upper chambers, and the inner store-rooms, and the place of propitiation, and the plan of the house of the Lord.  
\v 21 And see, \add here are\add* the courses of the priests and Levites for all the service of the house of the Lord, and \add there shall be\add* with you \add men\add* for every workmanship, and every one of ready skill in every art: also the chief men and all the people, \add ready\add* for all your commands.   
\c 29  
\p
\v 1 And David the king said to all the congregation, Solomon my son, whom the Lord has chosen, \add is\add* young and tender, and the work \add is\add* great; for \add it is\add* not for man, but for the Lord God.  
\v 2 I have prepared according to all \add my\add* might for the house of my God gold, silver, brass, iron, wood, onyx stones, and costly and variegated stones for setting, and every precious stone, and much Parian \add marble\add*.  
\v 3 And still farther, because I took pleasure in the house of my God, I have gold and silver which I have procured for myself, and, behold, I have given them to the house of my God over and above, beyond what I have prepared for the holy house.  
\v 4 Three thousand talents of gold of Suphir, and seven thousand talents of fine silver, for the overlaying of the walls of the sanctuary:  
\v 5 \add for you to use\add* the gold for \add things of\add* gold, and the silver for things of silver, and for every work by the hand of the artificers. And who is willing to dedicate himself in work this day for the Lord?   
\p
\v 6 Then the heads of families, and the princes of the children of Israel, and the captains of thousands and captains of hundreds, and the overseers of the works, and the king's builders, offered willingly.  
\v 7 And they gave for the works of the house of the Lord five thousand talents of gold, and ten thousand gold \add pieces\add*, and ten thousand talents of silver, and eighteen thousand talents of brass, and a hundred thousand talents of iron.  
\v 8 And those who had \add precious\add* stone, gave it into the treasuries of the house of the Lord by the hand of Jeiel the Gedsonite.  
\v 9 And the people rejoiced because of the willingness, for they offered willingly to the Lord with a full heart: and king David rejoiced greatly.   
\p
\v 10 And king David blessed the Lord before the congregation, saying,  
\p Blessed are you, O Lord God of Israel, our Father, from everlasting and to everlasting.  
\v 11 Yours, O Lord, \add is\add* the greatness, and the power, and the glory, and the victory, and the might: for you are Lord of all things that are in heaven and upon the earth: before your face every king and nation is troubled.  
\v 12 From you \add come\add* wealth and glory: you, O Lord, rule over all, the Lord of all dominion, and in your hand \add is\add* strength and rule; and \add you are\add* almighty with your hand to increase and establish all things.  
\v 13 And now, Lord, we give thanks to you, and praise your glorious name.  
\v 14 But who am I, and what \add is\add* my people, that we have been able to be thus forward \add in offering\add* to you? for all things \add are\add* yours, and of yours own have we given you,  
\v 15 for we are strangers before you, and sojourners, as all our fathers \add were\add*: our days upon the earth \add are\add* as a shadow, and there is no remaining.  
\v 16 O Lord our God, as for all this abundance which I have prepared that a house should be built to your holy name, it is of your hand, and all \add is\add* yours.  
\v 17 And I know, Lord, that you are He who searches the hearts, and you love righteousness. I have willingly offered all these things in simplicity of heart; and now I have seen with joy your people here present, willingly offering to you.  
\v 18 O Lord God of Abraham, and Isaac, and Israel, our fathers, preserve these things in the thought of the heart of your people for ever, and direct their hearts to you.  
\v 19 And to Solomon my son give a good heart, to perform your commandments, and \add to observe\add* your testimonies, and yours ordinances, and to accomplish the building of your house.   
\p
\v 20 And David said to the whole congregation, Bless you the Lord our God. And all the congregation blessed the Lord God of their fathers, and they bowed the knee and worshipped the Lord, and \add did homage\add* to the king.  
\v 21 And David sacrificed to the Lord, and offered up whole-burnt-offerings to the Lord on the morrow after the first day, a thousand calves, a thousand rams, a thousand lambs, and their drink-offerings, and sacrifices in abundance for all Israel.  
\v 22 And they ate and drank joyfully that day before the Lord: and they made Solomon the son of David king a second time, and anointed him king before the Lord, and Zadok to the priesthood.   
\p
\v 23 And Solomon sat upon the throne of his father David, and was highly honoured; and all Israel obeyed him.  
\v 24 The princes, and the mighty men, and all the sons of king David his father, were subject to him.  
\v 25 And the Lord magnified Solomon over all Israel, and gave him royal glory, such as was not upon any king before him.   
\p
\v 26 And David the son of Jesse reigned over Israel forty years;  
\v 27 seven years in Hebron, and thirty-three years in Jerusalem.  
\v 28 And he died in a good old age, full of days, in wealth, and glory: and Solomon his son reigned in his stead.  
\v 29 And the rest of the acts of David, the former and the latter, are written in the history of Samuel the seer, and in the history of Nathan the prophet, and in the history of Gad the seer,  
\v 30 concerning all his reign, and his power, and the times which went over him, and over Israel, and over all the kingdoms of the earth.   